COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[417,"§As-Sajdah\ndeeds\nList three of the calamities and trials with which Allah warned your people, then remind others of them.\nRecall a calamity that befell you, reckon yourself, and return to your Lord.\nFrom the stories of the Quran, review five of the worldly punishments inflicted on disobedient people.\nguid\nAllah's destruction of past generations is the greatest admonishment for those who have a mindful heart and insight.\nAsking to hasten the punishment is a sign of ignorance and recklessness.\nRepentance is not accepted when facing the punishment, or when seeing the angel of death at the hour of death.\nrefl\nوَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّن ذُكِّرَ بِـَٔايَٰتِ رَبِّهِۦ ثُمَّ أَعۡرَضَ عَنۡهَآۚ إِنَّا مِنَ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ مُنتَقِمُونَ ٢٢\n(And who does greater wrong), no one has done more wrong to himself than (one who is reminded of the verses of his Lord), His signs and proofs, (then turns away from them) by rejecting them, (We will surely take vengeance upon the criminals) for their rejection and turning away. Al-Qurtubi: 17/40-41.\nDescribe the risk of turning away from the Allah's admonishments, and its consequences?\nوَجَعَلۡنَا مِنۡهُمۡ أَئِمَّةٗ يَهۡدُونَ بِأَمۡرِنَا لَمَّا صَبَرُواْۖ وَكَانُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا يُوقِنُونَ ٢٤\nThis points to the qualities a preacher should acquire, such as being patient with the hardships of the worship, enduring calamities with patience, refraining patiently from worldly temptations, and believing with certainty in the signs. Whoever claims to be a preacher without acquiring these qualities, is misguided. Al-Alusi: 11/139.\nHow can a preacher become a leader of guidance?\nوَجَعَلۡنَا مِنۡهُمۡ أَئِمَّةٗ يَهۡدُونَ بِأَمۡرِنَا لَمَّا صَبَرُواْۖ\nSufyan was asked about the saying of Ali bin Abi Talib (t): \"Patience to the faith is like the head to a body,\" he replied: You have not heard what Allah says, (and We made some of them leaders, guiding by Our command when they observed patience), then, he says: \"When they took the head of the matter, they became heads themselves.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/446.\nFrom where did Ali bin Abi Talib (t) draw this meaning: \"Patience to the faith is like the head to a body\"?\nوَجَعَلۡنَا مِنۡهُمۡ أَئِمَّةٗ يَهۡدُونَ بِأَمۡرِنَا لَمَّا صَبَرُواْۖ وَكَانُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا يُوقِنُونَ ٢٤\n(When they observed patience), We made them leaders because they were patient with the duties of the religion, and endured trials. Moreover, it is said that they refrain patiently from worldly temptations. Al-Qurtubi: 17/43.\nWhat is meant by patience in this verse?\nأَوَ لَمۡ يَهۡدِ لَهُمۡ كَمۡ أَهۡلَكۡنَا مِن قَبۡلِهِم مِّنَ ٱلۡقُرُونِ يَمۡشُونَ فِي مَسَٰكِنِهِمۡۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٍۚ أَفَلَا يَسۡمَعُونَ ٢٦\n(Indeed in that are), in what is mentioned of Our destruction of past insolent nations, or in their remaining dwellings. (Signs): Great in themselves and numerous. (Then do they not listen) to these verses while reflecting and taking heed. Al-Alusi: 11/136.\nWhat is the benefit of mentioning the news of past nations?\nقُلۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡفَتۡحِ لَا يَنفَعُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ إِيمَٰنُهُمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يُنظَرُونَ ٢٩\nThose who claim that this refers to the conquest of Makkah went too far, and have made a grievous mistake, for on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) accepted those who became Muslims of the freed prisoners-of-war, who numbered nearly two thousand. If what was meant by this verse was the conquest of Makkah, he would not have accepted them, because Allah says: (Say, \"On the Day of Fath the belief of those who disbelieved will not benefit them, nor will they be given any respite\"). Hence, what is meant by Al-Fath here is Judgement. Ibn Kathir: 3/447.\nWhat is meant by Al-Fath in this verse?\nفَأَعۡرِضۡ عَنۡهُمۡ وَٱنتَظِرۡ إِنَّهُم مُّنتَظِرُونَ ٣٠\nTurn away from their foolishness, and reply to them as you have been commanded, (and wait, indeed, they are waiting), wait for the day of Fath; when Allah decides for you against them. Al-Qurtubi: 17/46.\nDescribe the style of the Quran in dealing with the deniers?\nwords\nالعَذَابِ الأَدنَىThe calamities and disasters in worldly life\nمِريَةٍDoubt\nمِن لِقَائِهِMeeting Moses (u) on the Night Journey\nأَوَ لَم يَهدِ لَهُمHas it not become clear to those deniers\nالجُرُزِA barren land, has no vegetation\nيُنظَرُونَThey will not be given any respite"],[418,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nSay, \"Allah suffices me, there is none worthy of worship but Him. I have placed my trust in Him, He is the Lord of the Majestic Throne.\"\nAsk Allah to be pleased with the Mothers of the believers, and know their rights.\nVisit your relatives and connect with them in any way you can.\nguid\nAllah enjoined on his Prophet to be pious so that no one would be proud to reject advice and reminder.\nDisbelievers and hypocrites are not fit to be consulted in matters of religion.\nWhoever relies on Allah, Allah will make for him a way out of every worry, a way out of every distress, and safety from every affliction.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ ٱتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ وَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمٗا ١\n(O Prophet), Allah is honoring him by addressing him by Prophethood, while He addressed all Prophets by their first names. Ibn Juzay: 2/181.\nIn this verse, Allah addresses His Prophet (ﷺ) in an honorable way. How?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ ٱتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ وَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَۚ\nAllah points out to something lower by referring to something higher. When He commands His servant and Messenger to do this, He is also commanding those who are lower than him, and the command is addressed to them more so. Ibn Kathir: 3/448.\nIs anyone above being commanded of piety, and prohibited from obeying the disbelievers and hypocrites?\nوَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَۚ\nThese are the real enemies, so do not obey them in some matters that undermine piety and are contrary to it. Al-Saadi: 657.\nAllah forbids the obedience of disbelievers and hypocrites. Why?\nوَٱتَّبِعۡ مَا يُوحَىٰٓ إِلَيۡكَ مِن رَّبِّكَۚ\nMeaning: Follow the Quran. This prohibits following the rituals of the age of ignorance (pre-Islam), and it enjoins Jihad against them. Moreover, it is a proof against following one’s desires with the existence of a clear text (command). This speech is directed to the Prophet (ﷺ) and his Ummah. Al-Qurtubi: 17/51.\nHow do you respond to one who abandons the Quran and follows his desires and people's opinions?\nوَمَا جَعَلَ أَدۡعِيَآءَكُمۡ أَبۡنَآءَكُمۡۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ قَوۡلُكُم بِأَفۡوَٰهِكُمۡۖ وَٱللَّهُ يَقُولُ ٱلۡحَقَّ وَهُوَ يَهۡدِي ٱلسَّبِيلَ ٤\nClaimed sons), adopted sons who carry the same as their adopting father. The reason for revealing this verse was that Zayd bin Haritha (t) was from a tribe called Kalb, and he was taken as captive by some Arabs, then was sold to Khadija (i), and she gave him to the Prophet (ﷺ) who adopted him as his son where he used to be called \"Zayd bin Muhammad\" until the revelation of this verse. Ibn Juzay: 2/182\nThis verse nullified one of the customs from the age of ignorance, what was it?\nٱلنَّبِيُّ أَوۡلَىٰ بِٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ مِنۡ أَنفُسِهِمۡۖ\nThan their own selves), let alone their own fathers, since the Prophet's rulings are binding to them, and obeying him is a duty for them, for he calls them to reason and wisdom, and enjoins them what saves them while their souls call them to follow their desires and worldly temptations, and enjoin them what ruins them. Al-Biqai: 15/290.\nWhy is the Prophet (ﷺ) closer to us than our own selves?\nوَأَزۡوَٰجُهُۥٓ أُمَّهَٰتُهُمۡۗ\nAllah has honored the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) by making them \"Mothers of the believers,\" which means treating them with veneration, reverence, and respect. Moreover, it is unlawful for them to marry anyone other than the Prophet (ﷺ). Al-Qurtubi: 17/62.\nGiven this verse, how do you respond to those innovators who belittle the Mothers of the believers?\nwords\nتُظَاهِرُونَ مِنهُنَّOne says to his wife: You are to me like the back of my mother\nأَدعِيَاءَكُمYour adopted sons\nوَمَوَالِيكُمYour allies in religion\nجُنَاحٌBlame\nأَولَى بِالمُؤمِنِينHe is closer to the believers than their own selves\nوَأَزوَاجُهُ أُمَّهَاتُهُمThe Prophet's wives are like the believers' mothers with regard to prohibiting marriage"],[419,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nReflect on the biographies of the Messengers with firm resolve, and write down the common qualities among them.\nRead about the Battle of Al-Ahzab to learn how Allah preserved the religion for us by making the Prophet and his Companions stand firm.\nSeek refuge with Allah from hypocrisy and hypocrites.\nguid\nThe Battle of the Trench was one of the most painful and tiring battles for Muslims.\nAllah afflicts His servants to make known the truthful from the untruthful.\nA hypocrite does no fulfill a covenant with the Creator, let alone a covenant with His creation.\nrefl\nوَإِذۡ أَخَذۡنَا مِنَ ٱلنَّبِيِّۧنَ مِيثَٰقَهُمۡ وَمِنكَ وَمِن نُّوحٖ وَإِبۡرَٰهِيمَ وَمُوسَىٰ وَعِيسَى ٱبۡنِ مَرۡيَمَۖ وَأَخَذۡنَا مِنۡهُم مِّيثَٰقًا غَلِيظٗا ٧\nAmong all Prophets, these five are singled out, because Allah caused them to exceed others. It is said that since they were the Messengers with firm resolve, the leaders of nations, and were given divine laws and Scriptures. Al-Qurtubi: 16/68.\nAmong all Prophets, these five are singled out. Why?\nوَإِذۡ أَخَذۡنَا مِنَ ٱلنَّبِيِّۧنَ مِيثَٰقَهُمۡ وَمِنكَ وَمِن نُّوحٖ وَإِبۡرَٰهِيمَ وَمُوسَىٰ وَعِيسَى ٱبۡنِ مَرۡيَمَۖ وَأَخَذۡنَا مِنۡهُم مِّيثَٰقًا غَلِيظٗا ٧ لِّيَسۡـَٔلَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ عَن صِدۡقِهِمۡۚ وَأَعَدَّ لِلۡكَٰفِرِينَ عَذَابًا أَلِيمٗا ٨\nAllah states that He took from the Prophets a solemn covenant and a binding pledge to support the religion of Allah and strive in His cause. Allah will question the Prophets and their followers about this solemn covenant: did they fulfill it and were they true to it, so that He might reward them with Paradise, or did they disbelieve, in which case He will inflict upon them the painful punishment. Al-Saadi: 659.\nAre the Prophets and Messengers the only ones who will be questioned about the solemn covenant?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَةَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡ إِذۡ جَآءَتۡكُمۡ جُنُودٞ فَأَرۡسَلۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ رِيحٗا وَجُنُودٗا لَّمۡ تَرَوۡهَاۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ بَصِيرًا ٩\nThis wind was a miracle for the Prophet (ﷺ), since he and the believers were situated across the trench from where it hit, but they were safe, and did not know about it. Al-Qurtubi: 16/90.\nDescribe the miracle of sending the wind during the Battle of Al-Ahzab.\nوَإِذۡ زَاغَتِ ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرُ وَبَلَغَتِ ٱلۡقُلُوبُ ٱلۡحَنَاجِرَ\n(And when eyes shifted in fear), their eyes stared in fright. It is said that their eyes focused only at the enemy. (And hearts reached the throats), their heart were dislocated to their throat in terror. Al-Baghawi: 3/544.\nThe description of the believers' eyes and hearts indicates something. What is it?\nإِذۡ جَآءُوكُم مِّن فَوۡقِكُمۡ وَمِنۡ أَسۡفَلَ مِنكُمۡ وَإِذۡ زَاغَتِ ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرُ وَبَلَغَتِ ٱلۡقُلُوبُ ٱلۡحَنَاجِرَ وَتَظُنُّونَ بِٱللَّهِ ٱلظُّنُونَا۠ ١٠\n(And you assumed about Allah assumptions), you thought the disbelievers would overpower you while Allah promised you victory over them. As for the hypocrites, they thought negatively and declared their thoughts, while the believers may had a passing thought that could not be evaded, then came to their senses and believed in Allah’s promise. Ibn Juzay: 2/183.\nWhat is the difference between the assumption of the believers and that of the hypocrites?\nوَإِذۡ يَقُولُ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقُونَ وَٱلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ مَّا وَعَدَنَا ٱللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُۥٓ إِلَّا غُرُورٗا ١٢\nApparently, the people with sickness in their hearts were not hypocrites. It is said that they were induced by the hypocrites through raising doubts to them. Moreover, it is said that they had weak faith because they were new to Islam. Al-Alusi: 11/156.\nWhat type of people do the hypocrites select for raising doubts to?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَت طَّآئِفَةٞ مِّنۡهُمۡ يَٰٓأَهۡلَ يَثۡرِبَ لَا مُقَامَ لَكُمۡ فَٱرۡجِعُواْۚ وَيَسۡتَـٔۡذِنُ فَرِيقٞ مِّنۡهُمُ ٱلنَّبِيَّ يَقُولُونَ إِنَّ بُيُوتَنَا عَوۡرَةٞ وَمَا هِيَ بِعَوۡرَةٍۖ إِن يُرِيدُونَ إِلَّا فِرَارٗا ١٣\n(A group of them), many of those with dead and sick hearts went around saying, (O people of Yathrib), departing from the beautiful names to which the Prophet (ﷺ) gave the city, Al-Madina and Taibah, and using its old name, Yathrib, which originates from the Arabic word (Tharab) that means blame and censure, in order to show their abandonment of Islam. Al-Biqai: 15/306.\nWhy did they use the old name of the city rather than the name given to it by the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nwords\nزَاغَتِ الأَبصَارُWhen eyes shifted in fear\nغُرُورًاDelusion\nيَثرِبَ\"Yathrib\", the old name for Al-Madina\nلاَ مُقَامَ لَكُمYou cannot withstand the enemy\nبُيُوتَنَا عَورَةٌOur homes are exposed\nأَقطَارِهَاThe surroundings of Al-Madina"],[420,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to protect you from misleading trials, both apparent and hidden.\nGlorify Allah, the Almighty, exalt Him, and praise Him as much as you can today.\nPractice an abandoned sunnah.\nguid\nFleeing adversity does not increase one's lifespan nor delay it, and may even bring a person closer to death unexpectedly.\nDiscouraging and obstruction of good are among the traits of hypocrites, hence beware of obstructing good and promoting evil.\nRemembrance of Allah, the Almighty, and the Hereafter often helps in following the example of the Prophet (ﷺ).\nrefl\nقُل لَّن يَنفَعَكُمُ ٱلۡفِرَارُ إِن فَرَرۡتُم مِّنَ ٱلۡمَوۡتِ أَوِ ٱلۡقَتۡلِ\nTaking proper measures of protection may benefit a person, if that is not contrary to the divine will and decree, but when the divine will and decree come to pass, then any measures will be to no avail, and every means one thinks could save him will not do so. Al-Saadi: 660.\nDoes this verse indicate the nullification of means?\nقُل لَّن يَنفَعَكُمُ ٱلۡفِرَارُ إِن فَرَرۡتُم مِّنَ ٱلۡمَوۡتِ أَوِ ٱلۡقَتۡلِ وَإِذٗا لَّا تُمَتَّعُونَ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ١٦\nThe aim of this verse is to instill awareness of the insignificance of this world to the Muslims, and redirect their ambitions toward the best through which they will attain eternal happiness by following Islamic teachings. Ibn Ashur: 21/291.\nThis verse contains a lesson for the Muslim to aspire for the Hereafter rather than this worldly life. Explain.\n۞قَدۡ يَعۡلَمُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمُعَوِّقِينَ مِنكُمۡ وَٱلۡقَآئِلِينَ لِإِخۡوَٰنِهِمۡ هَلُمَّ إِلَيۡنَاۖ وَلَا يَأۡتُونَ ٱلۡبَأۡسَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا ١٨\nMeaning: Those who discourage and prevent people from Jihad by their words and actions (who say to their brothers, \"Come and join us\") are the hypocrites who stayed behind in Al-Madina, and used to say to their relatives and to other hypocrites like them: Come and stay with us in Al-Madina, and abandon Jihad. Ibn Juzay: 2/184.\nIn this verse and beyond, Allah describes one of the traits of the hypocrites. Mention it.\nأَشِحَّةً عَلَيۡكُمۡۖ أَشِحَّةً عَلَى ٱلۡخَيۡرِۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَمۡ يُؤۡمِنُواْ\n(They are indisposed toward you), whether that is physical help, by joining the fight, or financial help, by spending on the cause. So, they do not engage in Jihad with their wealth or with their own selves. (Indisposed toward any good), what is expected of them. This is the worst thing a person can do, to be reluctant to do as he is instructed and to be stingy with his wealth and not spend it in the proper manner, stingy in terms of physical effort and refusing to engage with the enemies of Allah, or call people to the path of Allah, and stingy by refusing to benefit others by means of their position, knowledge, advice, or opinion. Al-Saadi: 661.\nList the types of stinginess that are meant by this verse.\nفَإِذَا جَآءَ ٱلۡخَوۡفُ رَأَيۡتَهُمۡ يَنظُرُونَ إِلَيۡكَ تَدُورُ أَعۡيُنُهُمۡ كَٱلَّذِي يُغۡشَىٰ عَلَيۡهِ مِنَ ٱلۡمَوۡتِۖ\nThis is a depiction of the way they see; they had the look of a scared and frightened person who stares at many directions in fear of a disaster striking him. Ibn Ashur: 21/297.\nThis verse describes one of the hypocrites’ traits that appears during times of fear. Mention it.\nلَّقَدۡ كَانَ لَكُمۡ فِي رَسُولِ ٱللَّهِ أُسۡوَةٌ حَسَنَةٞ لِّمَن كَانَ يَرۡجُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱلۡيَوۡمَ ٱلۡأٓخِرَ وَذَكَرَ ٱللَّهَ كَثِيرٗا ٢١\nThe scholars quoted this verse to prove that the Messenger's deeds constitute evidence for Sharia rulings, and that in principle his Ummah is subject to the same rulings as him, unless there is clear evidence to prove that some rulings are applicable to him alone. Al-Saadi: 661.\nAre the Prophet's (ﷺ) actions taken as evidence?\nوَلَمَّا رَءَا ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ٱلۡأَحۡزَابَ قَالُواْ هَٰذَا مَا وَعَدَنَا ٱللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُۥ وَصَدَقَ ٱللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُۥۚ وَمَا زَادَهُمۡ إِلَّآ إِيمَٰنٗا وَتَسۡلِيمٗا ٢٢\nThis indicates that faith can increase and become strong in accordance with people's circumstances, as the majority of scholars stated: faith can increase and decrease. Ibn Kathir: 3/457.\nDoes faith increase and decrease? Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nالمُعَوِّقِينَThose who discourage others from Jihad\nأَشِحَّةًUnwilling to offer any help\nتَدُورُ أَعيُنُهُمTheir eyes roll in fear\nسَلَقُوكُمThey accuse you\nحِدَادٍSharp tongues\nبَادُونIn the desert"],[421,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nStudy the biographies of some of the Companions; they are our role models.\nShare a message about the importance of steadfastness in the religion of Allah.\nAsk Allah to grant you truthfulness and keep you steadfast until you meet Him.\nguid\nThe Prophet's Companions have high status, great virtues, and Allah's purification of them. Whoever speaks ill of them, has denied the Quran.\nAllah's capability is limitless, as He is the Most Capable of all things, and nothing can escape Him.\nThe misdeed of the scholar and the noble is more severe than that of the ignorant and lowly.\nrefl\nمِّنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ رِجَالٞ صَدَقُواْ مَا عَٰهَدُواْ ٱللَّهَ عَلَيۡهِۖ فَمِنۡهُم مَّن قَضَىٰ نَحۡبَهُۥ وَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَنتَظِرُۖ وَمَا بَدَّلُواْ تَبۡدِيلٗا ٢٣\nThese are the real men, while others only appear outwardly to be men, as they have fallen short in terms of manly characteristics. Al-Saadi: 661.\nWhat is the reality of manhood?\nوَيُعَذِّبَ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ إِن شَآءَ أَوۡ يَتُوبَ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ غَفُورٗا رَّحِيمٗا ٢٤\nLinking their punishment to Allah's Will to indicate the vastness of Allah's mercy, and that He does not want them to lose hope in seeking His forgiveness through repentance so that He accepts it. Ibn Ashur: 21/309.\nIn this verse, why is the punishment linked to Allah's Will?\nوَيُعَذِّبَ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ إِن شَآءَ أَوۡ يَتُوبَ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ غَفُورٗا رَّحِيمٗا ٢٤\n(Or accept their repentance) by guiding them to repent and turn back to Him. This is more likely to be the case because Allah is the Most Generous. Hence, the verse ends with two divine names that are indicative of forgiveness, grace and kindness. Al-Saadi: 662.\nThis verse ends with Allah's Holy Names: The All-Forgiving, Most Merciful. Why?\nوَكَفَى ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٱلۡقِتَالَۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ قَوِيًّا عَزِيزٗا ٢٥\n(And Allah spared the believers from fighting) by sending upon their enemies wind and armies of angels until they fled, and their allies, Bani Quraithah, fled to their fortresses to be overcome by terror. Al-Qurtubi: 16/115.\nDue to Allah's Power and Might, He has armies that are known only to Him. Explain, given this verse.\nوَأَوۡرَثَكُمۡ أَرۡضَهُمۡ وَدِيَٰرَهُمۡ وَأَمۡوَٰلَهُمۡ وَأَرۡضٗا لَّمۡ تَطَـُٔوهَاۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٗا ٢٧\n(And a land on which you have not yet set foot), this was a promise of conquering a land on which Muslims had not yet set foot, such as Makkah, Yemen, the Levant, Iraq, and Egypt. Allah made the Muslims inherit all that plus what lies beyond them from the east and west. Ibn Juzay: 2/186.\nDescribe the miraculous aspect in this statement (And a land on which you have not yet set foot).\nوَإِن كُنتُنَّ تُرِدۡنَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ وَٱلدَّارَ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةَ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ أَعَدَّ لِلۡمُحۡسِنَٰتِ مِنكُنَّ أَجۡرًا عَظِيمٗا ٢٩\nGiving the choice to the Prophet's wives had many benefits, such as, showing their nobleness, high status, and firm resolve since they had chosen Allah, His Messenger, and the home of the Hereafter over the gains of this worldly life. Al-Saadi: 663.\nThis choice led to a higher status for the Mothers of the believers. Explain.\nيَٰنِسَآءَ ٱلنَّبِيِّ مَن يَأۡتِ مِنكُنَّ بِفَٰحِشَةٖ مُّبَيِّنَةٖ يُضَٰعَفۡ لَهَا ٱلۡعَذَابُ ضِعۡفَيۡنِۚ وَكَانَ ذَٰلِكَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ يَسِيرٗا ٣٠\nPunishments are commensurate with the level of sacred ordinances; violating a higher sacred ordinance warrants a higher punishment. Hence, the prescribed punishment for a free man is multiplied as opposed to that for a slave. The same thing is said about a married person as opposed to a single one. Al-Qurtubi: 16/133.\nDoes the sin become multiplied when committed by a person of higher status?\nwords\nقَضَى نَحبَهُFulfilled his pledge in defense of his religion, or died as a martyr\nبِغَيظِهِم لَم يَنَالُوا خَيرًاIn their rage without gaining any good\nظَاهَرُوهُمThose who supported them\nصَيَاصِيهِمTheir fortresses\nوَأُسَرِّحكُنَّI will divorce you\nبِفَاحِشَةٍ مُبَيِّنَةٍA clear sin"],[422,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nRemind your sisters not to be soft in speech when they need to talk to foreign men, or when speaking on the phone.\nShare a message about the importance of women abiding in their homes, especially nowadays.\nDedicate a special time on daily basis to read the Quran and some Hadiths of the Prophet (ﷺ).\nguid\nWomen's soft speech to men is risky.\nWomen's display of their charms as was done in the former days of ignorance is risky.\nReciting the Quran and noted supplications in homes protects them and their inhabitants from the evil ones among men and jinn.\nrefl\n۞وَمَن يَقۡنُتۡ مِنكُنَّ لِلَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَتَعۡمَلۡ صَٰلِحٗا نُّؤۡتِهَآ أَجۡرَهَا مَرَّتَيۡنِ وَأَعۡتَدۡنَا لَهَا رِزۡقٗا كَرِيمٗا ٣١\n(We will give her her reward twice), associating the reward with the pronoun (her) indicates the significance of the reward, which is fitting for her honorable status and well deserved. Multiplying the reward for their obedience is a way of honoring their status. Ibn Ashur: 22/5.\nIn light of this verse, describe the status of the Prophet's (ﷺ) wives.\nيَٰنِسَآءَ ٱلنَّبِيِّ لَسۡتُنَّ كَأَحَدٖ مِّنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ إِنِ ٱتَّقَيۡتُنَّۚ\nAllah has favored them over other women on the condition of piety. Since they had attained piety, they received the preference, except Fatima, the Messenger's (ﷺ) daughter, Mary, the daughter of Imran, and Asiya, Pharaoh's wife, because of the testimony of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) for each one of them that she was the chief of the women of her world. Ibn Juzay: 2/188.\nWhat is the condition for preferring the Mothers of the believers over other women? Who else had this distinction?\nفَلَا تَخۡضَعۡنَ بِٱلۡقَوۡلِ فَيَطۡمَعَ ٱلَّذِي فِي قَلۡبِهِۦ مَرَضٞ وَقُلۡنَ قَوۡلٗا مَّعۡرُوفٗا ٣٢\nThe sound heart has no desire for that which Allah has prohibited and can hardly be moved or stirred to desire even when there is a reason for that, because it is free of sickness. This is in contrast to the one who is sick at heart, who cannot cope with that which the sound-hearted person can cope with, and who cannot be patient like him. If there is the slightest reason that calls him to that which is prohibited, he will respond to it and will not refrain from it. Al-Saadi: 664.\nWhy is the sick heart singled out for mention?\nوَقُلۡنَ قَوۡلٗا مَّعۡرُوفٗا ٣٢\nSince Allah forbids women to speak softly, it may be thought that they are instructed to make their voices harsh. In order to ward off this notion, Allah says: (But speak in an appropriate manner), speak with a tone that is not harsh nor rough, just as it is not soft and alluring. Al-Saadi: 664\nThe verse ends with: (But speak in an appropriate manner), why?\nوَقَرۡنَ فِي بُيُوتِكُنَّ\nIt was said to Sauda bint Zam'a (i), a wife of the Prophet's (ﷺ): How come you do not go out? She replied: Allah commanded us to abide in our houses. Another wife of the Prophet's (ﷺ), Aisha bint Abi Bakr (i) used to weep whenever she read this verse because she participated in the battle of the Camel. Ibn Juzay: 2/188.\nHow did the Mothers of the believers abide by this verse?\nإِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ لِيُذۡهِبَ عَنكُمُ ٱلرِّجۡسَ أَهۡلَ ٱلۡبَيۡتِ\nThis is a clear statement that the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) are included among the members of his family (Ahl Al-Bayt) here, because they were the reason for revealing this verse, and the scholars unanimously agreed that they were the reason for the revelation in this case. Ibn Kathir: 3/465.\nHow does this verse nullify the Shia’s views on defining who Ahl Al-Bayt was?\nوَٱلصَّٰٓئِمِينَ وَٱلصَّٰٓئِمَٰتِ وَٱلۡحَٰفِظِينَ فُرُوجَهُمۡ وَٱلۡحَٰفِظَٰتِ\nFasting is also one of the greatest means of overcoming one's desires, it is quite apt that it should be mentioned next, (the men and the women who guard their chastity). Ibn Kathir: 3/469.\nGuarding chastity is mentioned right after fasting in this verse. Why?\nwords\nيَقنُت مِنكُنَّDevoutly obeys Allah and His Messenger\nوَأَعتَدنَاWe have prepared\nوَقَرنَAbide\nالرِّجسَHarm, sin, evil\nوَالقَانِتِينَThe obedient men\nوَالخَاشِعِينَThe humble men"],[423,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nRemember Allah today more than you did yesterday.\nAsk Allah to send His blessings upon the Prophet (ﷺ) in the morning and evening so that Allah will bless you.\nAttend a religious lesson or a lecture so the angels would ask Allah to send His blessings upon you.\nguid\nBeware of misinterpreting explicit commands according to desires; and it is imperative to submit and obey the commands of Sharia, as it is among the essentials of faith in Allah and the Prophet (ﷺ).\nBe aware that no one is above advice, admonition and reminding.\nAllah defends His Allies and preachers.\nrefl\nوَمَا كَانَ لِمُؤۡمِنٖ وَلَا مُؤۡمِنَةٍ إِذَا قَضَى ٱللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُۥٓ أَمۡرًا أَن يَكُونَ لَهُمُ ٱلۡخِيَرَةُ مِنۡ أَمۡرِهِمۡۗ\nMeaning: A believing man or woman should have no choice when it comes to anything decided by Allah and His Messenger; they must submit to the command of Allah and His messenger. Ibn Juzay: 2/189.\nWhat is the believer's duty when he finds out a proof from the Quran and Sunnah?\nوَإِذۡ تَقُولُ لِلَّذِيٓ أَنۡعَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِ وَأَنۡعَمۡتَ عَلَيۡهِ أَمۡسِكۡ عَلَيۡكَ زَوۡجَكَ وَٱتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ\nWhen someone seeks advice with regard to divorcing his wife, it is better to advise him to keep her as much as possible, because that is better than separation. Al-Saadi: 666.\nWhat advice should be given to one who intends to divorce his wife?\nوَتُخۡفِي فِي نَفۡسِكَ مَا ٱللَّهُ مُبۡدِيهِ وَتَخۡشَى ٱلنَّاسَ وَٱللَّهُ أَحَقُّ أَن تَخۡشَىٰهُۖ\nThe Messenger (ﷺ) conveyed the message clearly and did not leave anything of what was revealed to him but conveyed it, even this matter in which there was a rebuke to him. Al-Saadi: 666.\nThe Messenger (ﷺ) conveyed the message truthfully. How can we infer that from this verse?\nفَلَمَّا قَضَىٰ زَيۡدٞ مِّنۡهَا وَطَرٗا زَوَّجۡنَٰكَهَا لِكَيۡ لَا يَكُونَ عَلَى ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ حَرَجٞ فِيٓ أَزۡوَٰجِ أَدۡعِيَآئِهِمۡ إِذَا قَضَوۡاْ مِنۡهُنَّ وَطَرٗاۚ\nPractical teaching is more effective than verbal one, especially if it is also accompanied by words, for that is light upon light. Al-Saadi: 666.\nThe verse points to practical education. Explain\nمَّا كَانَ مُحَمَّدٌ أَبَآ أَحَدٖ مِّن رِّجَالِكُمۡ وَلَٰكِن رَّسُولَ ٱللَّهِ وَخَاتَمَ ٱلنَّبِيِّۧنَۗ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيۡءٍ عَلِيمٗا ٤٠\n(But he is the Messenger of Allah), when his fatherhood of any man is negated, this exception comes in order to avoid giving the wrong impression of non-existent ties between him and his Ummah, hence, they are reminded that since he is the Messenger of Allah, he is like a father figure to all of his Ummah through his compassion and mercy toward them, and their dutifulness and veneration of him as it is the case with every Prophet and his people. Ibn Ashur: 22/44.\nWhat is the benefit in stating this exception: (But he is the Messenger of Allah)?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱذۡكُرُواْ ٱللَّهَ ذِكۡرٗا كَثِيرٗا ٤١\nWhenever Allah enjoins His remembrance, He stipulates abundance, in contrast with other deeds. Remembrance of Allah is done by the heart and tongue, and has many varieties such as saying: None is worthy of worship but Allah; Glory be to Allah; Praise be to Allah; Allah is the greatest, and mentioning Allah's Holy Names. Ibn Juzay: 2/191.\nIn light of this verse, what is the advantage of Allah’s remembrance over all good deeds?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱذۡكُرُواْ ٱللَّهَ ذِكۡرٗا كَثِيرٗا ٤١\nAllah enjoins his servants to remember and thank Him abundantly for the blessings He bestowed upon them, and He does not set a limit for that due to its easiness and great reward. Ibn Abbas (t): No one is excused for not remembering Allah except one with a disabled mind. Al-Qurtubi: 16/167\nCan anyone be excused for not remembering Allah?\nwords\nقَضَىHe decided\nقَضَى زَيدٌ مِنهَا وَطَرًاZayd divorced her\nأَدعِيَائِهِمTheir adopted sons\nوَطَرًاNeed\nحَرَجٍA blame"],[424,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nHumbly greet those who are below you in age or status, may it be a reason for Allah's greeting to yon on the Day of Resurrection.\nAsk Allah to grant you sincerity and keep you from pretension in your calling to Islam, enjoining what is right and forbidding what is evil.\nGive glad tidings to your brethren of what Allah has prepared for them in terms of great reward for their patience in worshiping Allah and accepting His decree.\nguid\nThe Prophet's (ﷺ) status, rank and virtue is greater than the rest of the creation.\nCalling others to Allah is encouraged if the caller is qualified with the proper knowledge and forbearance.\nIt is forbidden to obey disbelievers, hypocrites, wrongdoers, and oppressors in any matter contrary to what is pleasing to Allah.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ إِنَّآ أَرۡسَلۡنَٰكَ شَٰهِدٗا وَمُبَشِّرٗا وَنَذِيرٗا ٤٥ وَدَاعِيًا إِلَى ٱللَّهِ بِإِذۡنِهِۦ وَسِرَاجٗا مُّنِيرٗا ٤٦\nThese descriptions that Allah gives of His Messenger Muhammad (ﷺ) reflect the purpose of his mission and its fundamental essence, which was unique to that message. Al-Saadi: 667.\nFive things are singled out for mention to describe our Prophet (ﷺ). Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ إِنَّآ أَرۡسَلۡنَٰكَ شَٰهِدٗا وَمُبَشِّرٗا وَنَذِيرٗا ٤٥\nGiving glad tidings precedes warning in the description of the Prophet (ﷺ) for he is more of a bearer of glad tidings than a warner, he is a mercy to the worlds and has the highest number of believing followers. Ibn Ashur: 22/53.\nGiving glad tidings precedes warning in the description of the Prophet (ﷺ). Why?\nوَدَاعِيًا إِلَى ٱللَّهِ\nBeing sincere in calling them to Allah alone, not to himself or seeking any kind of self-glory, as might be the inclination of many people in this situation. Al-Saadi: 668.\nFor preachers, some slips may occur with respect to sincerity. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَبَشِّرِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ بِأَنَّ لَهُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ فَضۡلٗا كَبِيرٗا ٤٧\nIbn Atiyah said: My father said to us: To me, this verse is the most promising in the Book of Allah because He commanded His Prophet to give glad tidings to the believers that they will have a great bounty from Allah, and He elucidates this great bounty by saying: (And those who have believed and done righteous deeds will be in meadows of the gardens in Paradise. They will have whatever they wish with their Lord; that is the great bounty) [42:22]. Al-Qurtubi: 16/173.\nSome scholars considered this verse to be among the most promising verses. Explain.\nوَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ وَدَعۡ أَذَىٰهُمۡ\n(And disregard their annoyance), since this may soften their hearts and encourage them to accept Islam, and it may put a stop to much of the harm that they do to Islam and its followers. Al-Saadi: 668.\nAllah forbids annoying the disbelievers. Why?\nوَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ وَدَعۡ أَذَىٰهُمۡ\nMeaning: Do not obey them in what they suggested of giving concessions in religion, nor help them. Al-Qurtubi: 16/173.\nThe disbelievers and hypocrites want from the preacher a particular thing. What is it?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا نَكَحۡتُمُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِ ثُمَّ طَلَّقۡتُمُوهُنَّ مِن قَبۡلِ أَن تَمَسُّوهُنَّ فَمَا لَكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِنَّ مِنۡ عِدَّةٖ تَعۡتَدُّونَهَاۖ فَمَتِّعُوهُنَّ وَسَرِّحُوهُنَّ سَرَاحٗا جَمِيلٗا ٤٩\nAllah commands their husbands to give them a gift in this case, so as to console them for leaving them, and so that the separation may be amicable. Al-Saadi: 668.\nWhat is the wisdom behind giving a gift to a divorced woman?\nwords\nتَمَسُّوهُنَّConsummating the marriage\nعِدَّةٍWaiting period for the woman\nتَعتَدُّونَهَاCounting for them\nوَسَرِّحُوهُنّDivorce them\nأَفَاءَ الله عَلَيكَAllah bestowed upon you\nخَالِصَةً لَكَExclusively for you"],[425,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nGive a talk or share a message on the risk of carelessness about the mixing of men and women.\nAsk Allah to grant you courage, wisdom, and good manners to say what is right.\nRemind a colleague that it is a good manner not to prolong a visit to preachers or scholars, as they may be busy.\nguid\nRemember that Allah, the Almighty, knows what is in your heart, therein store only what pleases Him, all Glory to Him.\nAcclimate yourself not to shy away from speaking the truth and calling to it.\nBeware of mixing with foreign women; every means of separating men from women is a purification of the hearts of both sides.\nrefl\nوَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَلِيمًا حَلِيمٗا ٥١\nAllah's Attribute of knowledge relates to the preceding statement: (And Allah knows what is in your hearts), while His Attribute of forbearance is meant to exhort the Messenger (ﷺ) to sustain this quality in the best of situations. Ibn Ashur: 22/77.\nThis verse concludes with the attribute of forbearance. Why?\nلَّا يَحِلُّ لَكَ ٱلنِّسَآءُ مِنۢ بَعۡدُ وَلَآ أَن تَبَدَّلَ بِهِنَّ مِنۡ أَزۡوَٰجٖ وَلَوۡ أَعۡجَبَكَ حُسۡنُهُنَّ\nHere, Allah shows His appreciation to the wives of His Messenger (ﷺ), as they had chosen Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ) and the final abode. Therefore, He had mercy on them and restricted His Messenger (ﷺ) to them, in the sense that he was not permitted to take any more wives. Al-Saadi: 670.\nThis verse contains an exhortation to give precedence to the Hereafter over the life of this world. How?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَدۡخُلُواْ بُيُوتَ ٱلنَّبِيِّ إِلَّآ أَن يُؤۡذَنَ لَكُمۡ إِلَىٰ طَعَامٍ غَيۡرَ نَٰظِرِينَ إِنَىٰهُ وَلَٰكِنۡ إِذَا دُعِيتُمۡ فَٱدۡخُلُواْ فَإِذَا طَعِمۡتُمۡ فَٱنتَشِرُواْ وَلَا مُسۡتَـٔۡنِسِينَ لِحَدِيثٍۚ إِنَّ ذَٰلِكُمۡ كَانَ يُؤۡذِي ٱلنَّبِيَّ فَيَسۡتَحۡيِۦ مِنكُمۡۖ\nIbn Abbas (k) said: This verse was revealed about some people who used to enter the Prophet's (ﷺ)house during his meal time and wait for it until it was ready, then, they ate and did not leave. So, they were commanded that they should not enter unless they were permitted to do so, and leave after eating, (and when you have eaten, disperse), leave the house. It is said that this is an etiquette taught to the ungracious by Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/194.\nThis verse contains some etiquettes of visitation. What are they?\nإِنَّ ذَٰلِكُمۡ كَانَ يُؤۡذِي ٱلنَّبِيَّ فَيَسۡتَحۡيِۦ مِنكُمۡۖ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يَسۡتَحۡيِۦ مِنَ ٱلۡحَقِّۚ\nWhen there is a clear instruction in Islamic teaching, even though one may think it is better to refrain from complying with it out of shyness, or to follow prevailing social etiquette, the right thing to do is to have the resolve to comply with the teachings and be certain that whatever is contrary to it is not in fact part of proper etiquette at all. Al-Saadi: 670.\nWhen people demand their rights set for them by Sharia, is that considered contrary to proper etiquette?\nوَإِذَا سَأَلۡتُمُوهُنَّ مَتَٰعٗا فَسۡـَٔلُوهُنَّ مِن وَرَآءِ حِجَابٖۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ أَطۡهَرُ لِقُلُوبِكُمۡ وَقُلُوبِهِنَّۚ\n(That is purer for your hearts and their hearts), pure from devilish temptations which cross the minds of men and women about each other, for looking at each other is a cause for temptation and desire. In some traditions, it is said that an evil glance is a poisoned arrow from Iblis. Al-Alusi: 11/248.\nWhat is the effect on men and women when they look at foreigners?\nوَإِذَا سَأَلۡتُمُوهُنَّ مَتَٰعٗا فَسۡـَٔلُوهُنَّ مِن وَرَآءِ حِجَابٖۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ أَطۡهَرُ لِقُلُوبِكُمۡ وَقُلُوبِهِنَّۚ\nBecause it is more appropriate, so as to avoid anything that could give rise to suspicion. The more one keeps away from things that could lead to evil, the safer it is, and the purer it is for one’s heart. Therefore, among the Islamic guidelines that Allah often explains in detail is the principle that all means that may cause evil or lead to it are prohibited, and it is prescribed to keep away from them by all possible means. Al-Saadi: 670.\nThe wisdom of Sharia is clear in prohibiting not only evil deeds but also everything that causes and leads to them. Briefly explain this concept in light of this verse.\nذَٰلِكُمۡ أَطۡهَرُ لِقُلُوبِكُمۡ وَقُلُوبِهِنَّۚ\nThe hearts of both groups are pure and full of piety, veneration of the sacred ordinances of Allah, and reverence for the Prophet (ﷺ). Since piety does not enable them to reach the level of infallibility, Allah intended to grant them more of it so the believers would attain levels of divine protection from devilish temptations by eliminating its causes. Moreover, this would bring the Mothers of the believers closer to the absolute infallibility of their husband (ﷺ). Virtuous deeds are for virtuous people by eliminating the causes of devilish temptations even presumably. Ibn Ashur: 22/91.\nWhat is the best way to purify the heart?\nwords\nتُرجِيPostpone the turn of whoever you wish of your wives\nوَتُؤوِيTake to yourself whom you will\nابتَغَيتَShare your time\nعَزَلتَWhose turn you have set aside\nنَاظِرِينَ إِنَاهُWaiting its readiness\nمَتَاعًاSomething, like a household item"],[426,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nPray often for Allah's blessings upon the Prophet (ﷺ).\nAsk forgiveness for your brothers and sisters in Islam, especially those whom you have hurt verbally or physically; humans are fallible.\nWrite a message about the benefits of hijab and its obligation.\nguid\nOne of the characteristics of hijab is that it hides the features of the woman so she becomes unrecognized.\nRemember that hypocrites are doomed to ruin.\nThe ways of Allah are set; they cannot be changed or altered.\nrefl\nلَّا جُنَاحَ عَلَيۡهِنَّ فِيٓ ءَابَآئِهِنَّ وَلَآ أَبۡنَآئِهِنَّ وَلَآ إِخۡوَٰنِهِنَّ وَلَآ أَبۡنَآءِ إِخۡوَٰنِهِنَّ وَلَآ أَبۡنَآءِ أَخَوَٰتِهِنَّ وَلَا نِسَآئِهِنَّ وَلَا مَا مَلَكَتۡ أَيۡمَٰنُهُنَّۗ وَٱتَّقِينَ ٱللَّهَۚ\nAt the end of this verse, Allah enjoins women to fear Him because they are more likely to be socially adept and less reserved, and Allah knows best. Al-Qurtubi: 18/213.\nAt the end of this verse, Allah enjoins women to fear Him. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ وَمَلَٰٓئِكَتَهُۥ يُصَلُّونَ عَلَى ٱلنَّبِيِّۚ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ صَلُّواْ عَلَيۡهِ وَسَلِّمُواْ تَسۡلِيمًا ٥٦\nAllah informs His servants about the rank of His servant and Prophet with Him, at the highest assembly of angels, that He praises him with the nearest angels to Him and the angels pray for him. Then, Allah enjoins the inhabitants of the lower world to invoke Allah’s blessings upon him and send him greetings of peace in order for him to have the praise of both worlds, the higher and lower. Ibn Kathir: 3/487.\nAfter He informs us that He confers His blessing upon the Prophet (ﷺ) and the angels pray for him, Allah enjoins to invoke His blessing and greeting upon him. why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡذُونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ لَعَنَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ وَأَعَدَّ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٗا مُّهِينٗا ٥٧\n(Those who offend Allah), this does not mean that harm can reach Allah since there is nothing can harm nor benefit Allah, the Almighty. It is said that it means offending the allies of Allah; however, the first interpretation is most probable, since it is narrated in Hadith that Allah says, \"The son of Adam slights Me, and he should not slight Me, and he disbelieves in Me, and he ought not to do so. As for his slighting Me, it is that he says that I have a wife and a son; and his disbelief in Me is his statement that I shall not resurrect him as I created him in the beginning.\" Ibn Juzay: 2/196.\nExplain how those disbelievers offended Allah.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡذُونَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِ بِغَيۡرِ مَا ٱكۡتَسَبُواْ فَقَدِ ٱحۡتَمَلُواْ بُهۡتَٰنٗا وَإِثۡمٗا مُّبِينٗا ٥٨\nThe sanctity of the believers is mentioned right after that of the Messenger (ﷺ) as a tribute to them, but they are mentioned separately to indicate that their ranking is lower than that of the Messenger (ﷺ). This digression is mentioned between the Prophet’s (ﷺ) sanctity rules and the etiquettes of his wives, daughters and the believing women. Ibn Ashur: 22/105.\nThe sanctity of the believers is mentioned right after that of the Messenger (ﷺ). Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ قُل لِّأَزۡوَٰجِكَ وَبَنَاتِكَ وَنِسَآءِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ يُدۡنِينَ عَلَيۡهِنَّ مِن جَلَٰبِيبِهِنَّۚ\nAllah instructs His Prophet (ﷺ) to instruct women in general to observe hijab, starting with his wives and daughters because the one who instructs others to do something should start with his family before anyone else, as Allah says: (O you who believe, protect yourselves and your families from a Fire) [66:6]. Al-Saadi: 672.\nWhat is the lesson learned for a preacher and a student of knowledge from this verse?\n۞لَّئِن لَّمۡ يَنتَهِ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقُونَ وَٱلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ وَٱلۡمُرۡجِفُونَ فِي ٱلۡمَدِينَةِ لَنُغۡرِيَنَّكَ بِهِمۡ ثُمَّ لَا يُجَاوِرُونَكَ فِيهَآ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ٦٠\nNo mention is made of the evil deed from which they should desist; therefore, this includes whatever thoughts they had in their minds that were calling to evil, whether that was slandering Islam and its followers, scaring the Muslims, undermining their resolve, speaking ill of the believing women and accusing them of immorality, or other sins that are committed by such people. Al-Saadi: 672.\nNo mention is made of the evil deed that is carried out by the hypocrites. Why?\n۞لَّئِن لَّمۡ يَنتَهِ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقُونَ وَٱلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ وَٱلۡمُرۡجِفُونَ فِي ٱلۡمَدِينَةِ لَنُغۡرِيَنَّكَ بِهِمۡ ثُمَّ لَا يُجَاوِرُونَكَ فِيهَآ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ٦٠\nThis indicates that banishing evildoers, who may cause harm by staying among the Muslims, is more effective in putting an end to their evil, and keeping it off. Al-Saadi: 672.\nThis verse contains a direction to avoid evildoers and keep them off. Explain.\nwords\nاحتَمَلُواThey bore the burden\nبُهتَانًاA slander\nيُدنِينَ عَلَيهِنّDraw veils over their heads, faces, and chests\nوَالمُرجِفُونَThose who spread rumors\nلَنُغرِيَنَّكَ بِهِمWe will surely incite you against them"],[427,"§Al-Ahzab\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, avert from us the punishment of Hell. Indeed, its punishment is ever adhering.\"\nDefend a righteous man who is falsely accused by writing a letter or an article, or by giving a speech.\nSay, \"O Allah, make my words right and guide my heart.\"\nguid\nDo not follow a chief or an elder in disobeying Allah; they will not avail you from Allah.\nBe kind to the servants of Allah, and do not harm a Muslim, especially scholars and reformers.\nThink of the enormity of the Trust that the son of Adam has assumed.\nrefl\nوَمَا يُدۡرِيكَ لَعَلَّ ٱلسَّاعَةَ تَكُونُ قَرِيبًا ٦٣ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَعَنَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ وَأَعَدَّ لَهُمۡ سَعِيرًا ٦٤\nThere is no benefit in knowing whether it will come sooner or later; what matters is loss and gain, doom or bliss, and whether a person deserves punishment or reward. This is what I can tell you about the Hour, and what I can say about who deserves what. Then Allah describes the punishment and those who deserve it, because the description given applies to those who deny the Hour, and says, (Indeed, Allah has cursed the disbelievers). Al-Saadi: 672.\nWhat is the prudence in mentioning the disbelievers' punishment after mentioning the coming of the Hour?\nيَوۡمَ تُقَلَّبُ وُجُوهُهُمۡ فِي ٱلنَّارِ يَقُولُونَ يَٰلَيۡتَنَآ أَطَعۡنَا ٱللَّهَ وَأَطَعۡنَا ٱلرَّسُولَا۠ ٦٦\nAmong all human limbs, the faces are singled out for mention since the fire's heat harms the faces more than it does the rest of the skin, as faces are the center of all delicate senses: Eyes, mouths, ears, and breathing. Allah says, (Then is he who will shield with his face the worst of the punishment on the Day of Resurrection) [39:24]. Ibn Ashur: 22/116.\nAmong all human limbs, the faces are singled out for mention. why?\nفَبَرَّأَهُ ٱللَّهُ مِمَّا قَالُواْۚ وَكَانَ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ وَجِيهٗا ٦٩\nIbn Abbas said: \"Moses (u) was close to Allah, for He answered all of his supplications.\"Alhasan said: \"Moses’ supplication was always answered.\" Moreover, it is said that Moses was loved and accepted. Al-Baghawi: 3/588.\nDescribe the rank of Moses (u) with his Lord, the Almighty.\nوَقُولُواْ قَوۡلٗا سَدِيدٗا ٧٠ يُصۡلِحۡ لَكُمۡ أَعۡمَٰلَكُمۡ وَيَغۡفِرۡ لَكُمۡ ذُنُوبَكُمۡۗ وَمَن يُطِعِ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ فَقَدۡ فَازَ فَوۡزًا عَظِيمًا ٧١\n(And say what is right), Ibn Abbas said: Say what is correct; Qatadah said: Say what is Just; Alhasan said: Say the truth. (He will amend for you your deeds), Ibn Abbas said: He will accept your good deeds. Muqatil said: He will purify your deeds. (And forgive you your sins. And whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger will surely achieve a supreme triumph), means that he will attain all the good. Al-Baghawi: 3/589.\nWhat are the good outcomes for protecting one's tongue and pursuing the right thing to say?\nإِنَّا عَرَضۡنَا ٱلۡأَمَانَةَ عَلَى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱلۡجِبَالِ فَأَبَيۡنَ أَن يَحۡمِلۡنَهَا وَأَشۡفَقۡنَ مِنۡهَا وَحَمَلَهَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُۖ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ ظَلُومٗا جَهُولٗا ٧٢\nThe Trust is the Sharia ordinances, which entail adhering to obedience and evading sins. Moreover, it is said, the trust with wealth; or washing after janabah (sexual impurity), but the most probable interpretation is the general Sharia ordinances. Ibn Juzay: 2/198.\nWhat is the Trust with which Allah entrusted us?\nإِنَّا عَرَضۡنَا ٱلۡأَمَانَةَ عَلَى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱلۡجِبَالِ فَأَبَيۡنَ أَن يَحۡمِلۡنَهَا وَأَشۡفَقۡنَ مِنۡهَا وَحَمَلَهَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُۖ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ ظَلُومٗا جَهُولٗا ٧٢\nAllah mentions the mountains right after the earth despite being part of it since the mountains are the biggest visible part of the earth, and people view its greatness. Ibn Ashur: 22/125.\nAllah mentions the mountains right after the earth despite being part of it. Why?\nإِنَّا عَرَضۡنَا ٱلۡأَمَانَةَ عَلَى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱلۡجِبَالِ فَأَبَيۡنَ أَن يَحۡمِلۡنَهَا وَأَشۡفَقۡنَ مِنۡهَا وَحَمَلَهَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُۖ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ ظَلُومٗا جَهُولٗا ٧٢ لِّيُعَذِّبَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقَٰتِ وَٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ وَٱلۡمُشۡرِكَٰتِ وَيَتُوبَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَى ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِۗ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ غَفُورٗا رَّحِيمَۢا ٧٣\nAllah emphasizes the great importance of the Trust which He has entrusted to those who are accountable. people are divided into three categories: Hypocrites, who pretend to fulfill it and adhere to it outwardly, but do not do so inwardly; polytheists who ignore it both outwardly and inwardly; and believers who fulfill it and adhere to it both outwardly and inwardly. Allah reveals the deeds of these three types of people, and what they will have of reward or punishment, as He says: (So that Allah will punish the hypocrite men and women, and the polytheist men and women, and Allah will accept the repentance of the believing men and women, for Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful). Al-Saadi: 674.\nWhat are the categories of people concerning the Trust?\nwords\nسَعِيرًاA blazing fire\nضِعفَينِDouble\nوَجِيهًاHighly honored\nسَدِيدًاTrue and just\nفَأَبَينَThey declined\nوَأَشفَقنَThey feared their violation of the Trust"],[428,"§Saba\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, recompense my good deeds with goodness, and my bad deeds with pardon and forgiveness.\"\nDo a new good deed today in the hope that Allah will forgive you and grant you generous provision.\nAttend an Islamic study circle in order to differentiate the truth from falsehood.\nguid\nWhoever gives much thanks to Allah in worldly life, will likely be grateful to Him in the Hereafter.\nBe among those who call for the religion of Allah and defend it, and beware of being among those who strive to avert people from it.\nThe Correct Shariah knowledge which is based on following the words of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet (ﷺ) leads to success in this world and the Hereafter.\nrefl\nٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي لَهُۥ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ\nThis Surah begins with (All praise be to Allah) to indicate that it contains signs of His Oneness and His great Attributes, which entail praising Him alone. Ibn Ashur: 22/135.\nThis Surah begins with (All praise be to Allah). Why?\nٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي لَهُۥ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ\n(To Whom belongs all that is in the heavens and all that is on earth), this relative clause is an allusion to the denial of the polytheists who praised other things that did not have the least influence or awareness of these worlds, and forgot to praise the One Who owns them and everything else in them. Ibn Ashur: 22/136.\nWhy is a relative clause used in this verse?\nوَلَهُ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۚ\nBecause in the Hereafter He will be praised and extolled in a manner that He was not praised and extolled in this world. When Allah judges between all creatures, and people and all creatures see His verdict and recognize the perfect nature of his justice, fairness, and wisdom, they will all praise Him for that, even those who are faced with punishment and are doomed to enter Hell, their hearts will be filled with praise for Him, and they will know that the punishment is the consequence of their deeds and that He is just in His ruling to punish them. Al-Saadi: 674.\nWhy is praising Allah in the Hereafter is mentioned?\nعَٰلِمِ ٱلۡغَيۡبِۖ لَا يَعۡزُبُ عَنۡهُ مِثۡقَالُ ذَرَّةٖ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَلَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَلَآ أَصۡغَرُ مِن ذَٰلِكَ وَلَآ أَكۡبَرُ إِلَّا فِي كِتَٰبٖ مُّبِينٖ ٣\n(Not absent from Him), nothing is hidden from Him, that is, everything is encompassed by His knowledge, and nothing is concealed from Him. Even though bones may be scattered and disintegrate, He knows where they have gone and where they have dispersed, then He will bring them back just as He created them the first time because He has knowledge of all things. Ibn Kathir: 3/504.\nAfter mentioning the resurrection, Allah is described as the Knower of the unseen. Why?\nوَيَرَى ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكَ مِن رَّبِّكَ هُوَ ٱلۡحَقَّ\nUsing the word, (see), instead of \"know\" to indicate that their knowledge is as certain as seeing. Ibn Ashur: 22/145.\nIn this verse, the word, (see) is used instead of “know”. Why?\nوَيَرَى ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكَ مِن رَّبِّكَ هُوَ ٱلۡحَقَّ وَيَهۡدِيٓ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡحَمِيدِ ٦\nAmong Allah's Attributes, these two (the Exalted in Might, the Praiseworthy) are used to indicate that when the believers deem the Quran as the true guidance, they realize through their faith that this path leads them to might; Allah says, (All might belongs to Allah and His Messenger, and the believers) [63:8]. Ibn Ashur: 22/146.\nIn this verse, Allah’s Attributes, (the Exalted in Might, the Praiseworthy) are used. Why?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ هَلۡ نَدُلُّكُمۡ عَلَىٰ رَجُلٖ يُنَبِّئُكُمۡ إِذَا مُزِّقۡتُمۡ كُلَّ مُمَزَّقٍ إِنَّكُمۡ لَفِي خَلۡقٖ جَدِيدٍ ٧\nIf you say: Allah's Messenger was prominent and well-known in his tribe, Quraish, and his preaching about resurrection was prevalent among them, so, what is the meaning of their saying, (Shall we show you a man), referring to him as an unknown person who says unknown things? I say: They said that in ridicule and mockery for the purpose of laughter and disregard of him (ﷺ) and his message. Al-Qurtubi: 17/257.\nWhy did they ignore the Prophet’s (ﷺ) Message by calling him just (a man)?\nwords\nيَلِجُGoes into\nيَعرُجُAscends\nلاَ يَعزُبُNot absent from Him\nعَذَابٌ مِن رِجزٍ أَلِيمٌA punishment of agonizing pain\nمُزِّقتُمYou died and your bodies disintegrated"],[429,"§Saba\ndeeds\nPerform all your duties today in a way that is pleasing to Allah, the Almighty.\nTeach a Muslim a surah from the Quran in gratitude to Allah for memorizing the surah.\nSay, \"O Allah, make me among your grateful servants.\"\nguid\nTurning in repentance to Allah is a cause for benefiting from the universal signs.\nHave a trade or master a skill so you become self-sufficient.\nThe unseen is known only to Allah, the Almighty.\nrefl\nأَفَلَمۡ يَرَوۡاْ إِلَىٰ مَا بَيۡنَ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَمَا خَلۡفَهُم مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ إِن نَّشَأۡ نَخۡسِفۡ بِهِمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ أَوۡ نُسۡقِطۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡ كِسَفٗا مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِۚ\nAllah reveals that the One who is capable of creating the heavens and earth and everything in them, is capable of resurrecting the disbelievers and hastening their punishment. So, Allah uses the fact of His overwhelming power as evidence for this argument. Since they are surrounded by the heavens and earth which belong to Him, how can they be safe from being swallowed by the earth or hit by fragments from the heavens, similar to what happened to Korah and the people of the Thicket? Al-Qurtubi: 17/259.\nAllah's capability of creating the heavens and earth is evidence of His ability to punish the disobedient. How?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَةٗ لِّكُلِّ عَبۡدٖ مُّنِيبٖ ٩\nThe more a person turns to Allah in repentance, the greater he will benefit from the signs, because the one who repents and turns to his Lord focuses with all his heart and aspirations on his Lord, and turns to Him in all his affairs. Thus, he becomes close to his Lord and has no concern or interest except to strive to please Him. So, when he looks at created beings, it is in order to reflect and learn, not with heedlessness in a manner that is of no benefit. Al-Saadi: 676.\nThose who turn to Allah in repentance benefit from the signs. Why?\n۞وَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا دَاوُۥدَ مِنَّا فَضۡلٗاۖ يَٰجِبَالُ أَوِّبِي مَعَهُۥ وَٱلطَّيۡرَۖ وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلۡحَدِيدَ ١٠\nThe word, (bounty) is in an indefinite form to indicate its greatness, which is the bounty of Prophethood, kingship, the attendance to reforming his people, justice in judgment, bravery in battlefield, abundance of provision, lack of need for people due to his making of metal coats of mail taught to him by Allah, receiving the Psalms, having a beautiful voice, and living a long righteous life, etc. Ibn Ashur: 22/155.\nThe word, (bounty) is in an indefinite form. Why?\nأَنِ ٱعۡمَلۡ سَٰبِغَٰتٖ وَقَدِّرۡ فِي ٱلسَّرۡدِۖ وَٱعۡمَلُواْ صَٰلِحًاۖ إِنِّي بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ بَصِيرٞ ١١\nThis verse proves that learning trades by people of virtue does not lessen their status, rather, it enhances their virtues since they attain modesty, become self-sufficient, and earn halal provision without favor from others. Al-Qurtubi: 17/263.\nDoes learning trades or mastering skills by a student of knowledge lessen his status?\nٱعۡمَلُوٓاْ ءَالَ دَاوُۥدَ شُكۡرٗاۚ\nThis proves that showing gratitude can be through deeds as well as words and intention. An Arab poet said: My gratitude to you for your favor are three: My hand, my tongue, and my heart. Ibn Kathir: 3/507.\nWhat are the different ways for man to show his gratitude to his Lord?\nٱعۡمَلُوٓاْ ءَالَ دَاوُۥدَ شُكۡرٗاۚ وَقَلِيلٞ مِّنۡ عِبَادِيَ ٱلشَّكُورُ ١٣\nIt is narrated that David (u) said: O Lord, how can I thank you for your blessings when my ability to and inspiration to do so is in itself a blessing by you? Allah replied: O David, only now you knew Me. The reality of gratitude for a blessing is acknowledging its Bestower and applying it in His obedience -and few people do that- while ingratitude is using the blessing in His disobedience. Al-Qurtubi: 17/278.\nWhat is the reality of gratitude? Are there many grateful people?\nفَلَمَّا قَضَيۡنَا عَلَيۡهِ ٱلۡمَوۡتَ مَا دَلَّهُمۡ عَلَىٰ مَوۡتِهِۦٓ إِلَّا دَآبَّةُ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ تَأۡكُلُ مِنسَأَتَهُۥۖ فَلَمَّا خَرَّ تَبَيَّنَتِ ٱلۡجِنُّ أَن لَّوۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٱلۡغَيۡبَ مَا لَبِثُواْ فِي ٱلۡعَذَابِ ٱلۡمُهِينِ ١٤\nMeaning: It became apparent to the people that jinn do not know the unseen. It is said that (realized), knew. Ibn Juzay: 2/203.\nHow do you respond to those who claim that jinn know the unseen?\nwords\nكِسَفًاFragments\nمُنِيبٍOne who turns to Allah in repentance\nأَوِّبِي مَعَهُEcho Allah's praise with him\nوَقَدِّر فِي السَّردِMaintain balance in the linking rings of the coats of mail\nعَينَ القِطرِA spring of liquid copper\nوَجِفَانٍ كَالجَوَابِBowls like reservoirs"],[430,"§Saba\ndeeds\nMention Allah's name before eating and thank him after in gratitude.\nFrom the verses about the story of Sheba, list three consequences for being ungrateful for Allah’s blessings.\nShare a message with your relatives and friends in which you remind them of the divine punishments for those who turn away from the religion of Allah.\nguid\nBeware of being ungrateful for Allah's blessings.\nPray for what will benefit you and beware of praying for what will cause you harm.\nBeware of the devil's whispers and temptations.\nrefl\nلَقَدۡ كَانَ لِسَبَإٖ فِي مَسۡكَنِهِمۡ ءَايَةٞۖ\nThe mention of Solomon (u) brought the mention of Sheba due to the contact between the two kingdoms through the story of the Queen of Sheba, and the disparity between them, where the kingdom of David and Solomon (p) was an example of ample bestowal of blessings upon the grateful while the kingdom of Sheba was an example of dispossession of blessings from the ungrateful. Ibn Ashur: 22/165.\nThe story of Sheba is mentioned right after the story of Solomon (u). Why?\nفَأَعۡرَضُواْ فَأَرۡسَلۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ سَيۡلَ ٱلۡعَرِمِ وَبَدَّلۡنَٰهُم بِجَنَّتَيۡهِمۡ جَنَّتَيۡنِ ذَوَاتَيۡ أُكُلٍ خَمۡطٖ وَأَثۡلٖ وَشَيۡءٖ مِّن سِدۡرٖ قَلِيلٖ ١٦\n(But they turned away), they turned away from offering gratitude to Allah, or from obeying the Prophets. Ibn Juzay: 2/203. Question: The people of Sheba turned away from a matter, which caused their ruin. What was it? Question: Why is a relative clause used in this verse?\nوَبَدَّلۡنَٰهُم بِجَنَّتَيۡهِمۡ جَنَّتَيۡنِ ذَوَاتَيۡ أُكُلٍ خَمۡطٖ وَأَثۡلٖ وَشَيۡءٖ مِّن سِدۡرٖ قَلِيلٖ ١٦\nThis is a befitting recompense for their deeds; just as they replaced gratitude with ingratitude, those blessings were replaced with the things mentioned. Al-Saadi: 677.\nGiven this verse, discuss this principle: (The requital befits the action).\nوَجَعَلۡنَا بَيۡنَهُمۡ وَبَيۡنَ ٱلۡقُرَى ٱلَّتِي بَٰرَكۡنَا فِيهَا قُرٗى ظَٰهِرَةٗ وَقَدَّرۡنَا فِيهَا ٱلسَّيۡرَۖ سِيرُواْ فِيهَا لَيَالِيَ وَأَيَّامًا ءَامِنِينَ ١٨\nAnd We determined between them the [distances of] journey): It is said that a traveler on any road would spend the night in one city, and take a midday nap in another. (Travel...in safety), We said to them: Travel without fear from bandits, hunger, thirst or travel hardships. Ibn Atiyah: 4/416.\nIn this verse, what is meant by (Travel...in safety)?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٖ شَكُورٖ ١٩\nThe word, (signs) is in plural form since the story has many signs and lessons. Their dwelling place was a sign of Allah's capability, mercy, and bounty. Sending a devastating torrent against them was a sign of Allah's sole control and retaliation. The shift in their state from prosperity to adversity was a sign of fluctuating conditions and a changing world, which is a sign of not being complacent during times of prosperity and hardship. The development of their region and expansion of their cities to the Levant was a sign of high civilization and great sovereignty, and that security is the basis for development. Their wish for the cessation of all that was a sign of declining minds that led to the deterioration of the nation's affairs and its downfall. Abandonment of their homes and dispersion throughout the land was a sign of how hardships may drive people to expose themselves to danger and suffering. Combining the two traits (patient) and (grateful) to indicate that the believer must adhere to attain these traits: Patience over hardships, and gratitude for Allah's blessings. These people were not grateful for the blessings and hence became insolent in them, and were not patient over the hardship of losing the blessings. Ibn Ashur: 22/180.\nThe word, (signs) is in plural form. Why? The verse concludes with (patient) & (grateful). Why?\nوَلَقَدۡ صَدَّقَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ إِبۡلِيسُ ظَنَّهُۥ فَٱتَّبَعُوهُ إِلَّا فَرِيقٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٢٠\nIbn Qutaybah said: When Iblees was granted respite by Allah, he said: I will deceive and mislead them, and he was not sure of that, but when they followed and obeyed him, his assumption became true. Alhasan said: Iblees did not wave a sword at them nor lashed them with a whip, rather, he promised and aroused in them false hopes so they became deluded. Al-Baghawi: 3/604.\nExplain how Iblees found his assumption about them to be true.\nوَمَا كَانَ لَهُۥ عَلَيۡهِم مِّن سُلۡطَٰنٍ إِلَّا لِنَعۡلَمَ مَن يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ مِمَّنۡ هُوَ مِنۡهَا فِي شَكّٖۗ وَرَبُّكَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٍ حَفِيظٞ ٢١\nIblees did not force them to disbelief, but he called them to sins and made sins alluring to them. He did not provide proof for them to follow, rather, they followed him of their lustful desires, imitation of other disbelievers, and their own whims. Al-Baghawi: 3/604.\nCan Iblees force man to disbelieve or commit sins?\nwords\nآيَةٌA sign of Our power\nذَوَاتَيConsisted of\nسَيلَ العَرِمِA devastating torrent that destroyed the dam and flooded their gardens\nأُكُلٍ خَمطٍA bitter fruit\nوَأَثلٍTamarisk bushes, with no fruit\nسِدرٍLote trees, with thorns"],[431,"§Saba\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to make you intercede for your loved ones.\nAsk Allah to make His Prophets, angels, and righteous people intercede for you, and do not ask for intercession from anyone else, no matter who he is.\nThank Allah, the Almighty, for the provision He has provided for you.\nguid\nAsk Allah to fill your heart with fear of Him, glory to Him, and love for Him.\nRemember that the provider of provision is Allah alone, so do not ask anyone else.\nWhen calling others to Allah, give good tidings of good and warning against evil.\nrefl\nوَلَا تَنفَعُ ٱلشَّفَٰعَةُ عِندَهُۥٓ إِلَّا لِمَنۡ أَذِنَ لَهُۥۚ\nAllah points out that even the angels, with their high status, cannot intercede for anyone until they are permitted to do so. When they are given permission and heard, they become in a state of shock and remain in that state. If that is the case with the angels, then, how will the idols intercede? Or, how can you (the polytheists) hope for the idols' intercession while you do not believe in the Day of Resurrection? Al-Qurtubi: 17/311.\nGiven this verse, describe the significance of intercession with Allah on the Day of Resurrection.\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَن قُلُوبِهِمۡ قَالُواْ مَاذَا قَالَ رَبُّكُمۡۖ قَالُواْ ٱلۡحَقَّۖ وَهُوَ ٱلۡعَلِيُّ ٱلۡكَبِيرُ ٢٣\nMany Prophetic Hadiths affirm that this verse talks about the angels (p); when they hear the revelation of the words of to the angel Gabriel, they become terrified, then when their hearts are relieved of dread, they say to each other: \"What did your Lord just say?\" They say, \"The Truth.\" Ibn Juzay: 2/205.\nThis verse proves the significance of the revelation from Allah. Explain.\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَن قُلُوبِهِمۡ قَالُواْ مَاذَا قَالَ رَبُّكُمۡۖ قَالُواْ ٱلۡحَقَّۖ وَهُوَ ٱلۡعَلِيُّ ٱلۡكَبِيرُ ٢٣\n(He is the Most High, Most Great), the mention of these two attributes of Allah is appropriate to the answer, which means that Allah decrees what is right for every deserving soul, as the condition of everyone is not hidden from Him, and nothing can prevent Him from giving everyone his right. Ibn Ashur: 22/190-191.\nWhat is the benefit of mentioning these two attributes, (the Most High, Most Great) in this verse?\nوَإِنَّآ أَوۡ إِيَّاكُمۡ لَعَلَىٰ هُدًى أَوۡ فِي ضَلَٰلٖ مُّبِينٖ ٢٤\nMeaning: One of the two sides must be speaking falsehood, and the other must be telling the truth. There is no way that you and we could both be following true guidance, or could both be misguided. Only one of us can be correct. Ibn Kathir: 3/516.\nWhat do you think about one who belittles the differences among sects and religions, and believes that each one is correct?\nقُلۡ يَجۡمَعُ بَيۡنَنَا رَبُّنَا ثُمَّ يَفۡتَحُ بَيۡنَنَا بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَهُوَ ٱلۡفَتَّاحُ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٢٦\nAllah's attributes: (The All-Knowing) and (Judge) are joined together to affirm that His judgment is the absolute justice because He is the All-Knowing, where His judgment is never affected by lack of knowledge, incompetence, or weakness that stems from ignorance of conditions and consequences. Ibn Ashur: 22/195.\nAllah's attributes: (The All-Knowing) and (Judge) are mentioned together. Why?\nوَمَآ أَرۡسَلۡنَٰكَ إِلَّا كَآفَّةٗ لِّلنَّاسِ بَشِيرٗا وَنَذِيرٗا وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٢٨\nThis is a declaration from Allah that He sent Muhammad (ﷺ) to all mankind, and this is one of the attributes of which Allah distinguished Muhammad (ﷺ) among all the Prophets. Ibn Atiyah: 4/420.\nThe verse mentions a special attribute of our Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ). What is it?\nوَلَوۡ تَرَىٰٓ إِذِ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ مَوۡقُوفُونَ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ يَرۡجِعُ بَعۡضُهُمۡ إِلَىٰ بَعۡضٍ ٱلۡقَوۡلَ يَقُولُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتُضۡعِفُواْ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ لَوۡلَآ أَنتُمۡ لَكُنَّا مُؤۡمِنِينَ ٣١\nIf only you could see) O Muhammad (when the wrongdoers would be made to stand before their Lord), they will be detained for reckoning, blaming and reproaching each other after they used to be helpful friends in worldly life. The result of the conditional statement (If only you could see) is dropped, which means that you would see a horrible and terrifying sight. Al-Qurtubi: 17/316.\nDescribe the condition of the polytheists' friends when they will be made to stand before Allah.\nwords\nفُزِّعَTheir hearts are relieved of dread\nيَفتَحُHe judges\nبِالحَقِّWith justice\nالفَتَّاحُThe Supreme Judge over His creation\nوَلاَ بِالَّذِي بَينَ يَدَيهِThe Scriptures that preceded the Holy Quran\nمَوقُوفُونThey will be detained for reckoning\nيَرجِعُThey will quarrel with each other"],[432,"§Saba\ndeeds\nFast a day for the sake of Allah.\nSay: \"O Allah, make us grateful in times of prosperity and patient in times of adversity.\"\nSpend some of your money to support a preaching endeavor with the hope of compensation from Allah, the Almighty.\nguid\nAvoid obeying the chiefs in falsehood.\nBeware of friendship with hypocrites; they are cunning and try to avert you from obeying Allah with all kinds of tricks.\nRemember that the people of disbelief and disobedience will have a great regret when they see the punishment.\nrefl\nقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتُضۡعِفُوٓاْ أَنَحۡنُ صَدَدۡنَٰكُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡهُدَىٰ بَعۡدَ إِذۡ جَآءَكُمۖ بَلۡ كُنتُم مُّجۡرِمِينَ ٣٢\nMeaning: We did nothing more than to call you, and you followed us without evidence or proof, and you went against the evidence and proof which the Messengers brought because of your own desires; it was your own choice. Hence, they will say: (Rather, you were criminals). Ibn Kathir: 3/518.\nThe oppressed will be described as criminals. Why?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتُضۡعِفُواْ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ بَلۡ مَكۡرُ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ إِذۡ تَأۡمُرُونَنَآ أَن نَّكۡفُرَ بِٱللَّهِ وَنَجۡعَلَ لَهُۥٓ أَندَادٗاۚ\nMeaning: The oppressed will say to the arrogant: It was your conspiracy of night and day that caused us to be disbelievers. Ibn Juzay: 2/207. Question: Every allegiance that is not based on Allah's Sharia will turn into enmity. Give an example of that in light of this verse. Question: Why is a relative clause used in this verse?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتُضۡعِفُواْ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ بَلۡ مَكۡرُ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ إِذۡ تَأۡمُرُونَنَآ أَن نَّكۡفُرَ بِٱللَّهِ وَنَجۡعَلَ لَهُۥٓ أَندَادٗاۚ\nThis is the reply of the followers to their leaders when they said to them: You disbelieved by your own choice. The oppressed reply is: Rather, we disbelieved because you conspired against us night and day. The conspiracy is associated with night and day to indicate diligence and continuity. Ibn Atiyah: 4/421.\nWhat will be the reply of the oppressed to their misguiding leaders on the Day of Resurrection?\nوَأَسَرُّواْ ٱلنَّدَامَةَ لَمَّا رَأَوُاْ ٱلۡعَذَابَۚ\nMeaning: They will realize that the argument that they tried to use against one another in order to be saved from the punishment is invalid, and that they are all wrongdoers who deserve punishment. Hence, each one of them will be filled with deep remorse and will wish that he had followed the truth, and rejected the falsehood that brought him to this punishment. However, each one will keep this regret to himself for fear of scandal and shame if he admits that he deserves it. Al-Saadi: 681.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, the disbelievers will keep their regrets to themselves. Why?\nوَقَالُواْ نَحۡنُ أَكۡثَرُ أَمۡوَٰلٗا وَأَوۡلَٰدٗا وَمَا نَحۡنُ بِمُعَذَّبِينَ ٣٥\nMeaning: They were proud of their great wealth and great number of children, and they believed that this was a sign that Allah loved them and cared for them, and that if He gave them this in this world, He would not punish them in the Hereafter. Ibn Kathir: 3/519.\nThe disbelievers linked the abundance of wealth and children to the absence of punishment. Why?\nقُلۡ إِنَّ رَبِّي يَبۡسُطُ ٱلرِّزۡقَ لِمَن يَشَآءُ وَيَقۡدِرُ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٦\nIn an implicit reply to them, Allah makes known that He extends provision in this life and restricts it in accordance with His will. Hence, He may extend provision for a disbeliever and disobedient, while restricts it for a believer and obedient, or He can do the opposite. So, there is no proof that this is linked to what will occur in the Hereafter. Ibn Juzay: 2/208.\nWhat is the way of Allah in distributing provisions in this life? Is it a true criteria for salvation in the Hereafter?\nوَمَآ أَنفَقۡتُم مِّن شَيۡءٖ فَهُوَ يُخۡلِفُهُۥۖ وَهُوَ خَيۡرُ ٱلرَّٰزِقِينَ ٣٩\nIbn Al-Arabi said: \"Allah may compensate the same or more, and He may compensate it in this life or keep it as a reward in the Hereafter. The same arrangement is done with the supplication when Allah promises to answer it.\" I said: Allah may compensate it as good health or a long life. Allah has great secrets in His creation. Ibn Ashur: 22/221.\nList various types of compensation that Allah may give to His servant when he spends.\nwords\nالنَّدَامَةَRegret\nيَبسُطُExtends\nزُلفَىNearer\nالغُرُفَاتHigh dwellings in Paradise\nمُعَاجِزِينَSeeking to discredit\nمُحضَرُونَThey will be brought into the punishment\nوَيَقدِرُ لَهُRestricts it for him"],[433,"§Saba\ndeeds\nTestify to the Oneness of Allah, intending to renounce every god other than Allah, the Almighty.\nShare a message with your family or peers, in which you warn against witchcraft and going to sorcerers, explaining that this is contrary to the worship of Allah.\nMake time for yourself and read a surah from the Holy Quran.\nguid\nExalt, praise, and glorify Allah, especially when hearing what detracts from His Greatness and Majesty, following the example of the nearest angels to Him.\nRevive in yourself the worship of reflection, as it is one of the most important acts of worship of the heart.\nDo not use religion as means to attain the perishable gains of worldly life, for the Hereafter is better and everlasting.\nrefl\nوَيَوۡمَ يَحۡشُرُهُمۡ جَمِيعٗا ثُمَّ يَقُولُ لِلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ أَهَٰٓؤُلَآءِ إِيَّاكُمۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡبُدُونَ ٤٠\nMeaning: Allah states that on the Day of Resurrection, He will rebuke the idolators before all creation. He will ask the angels whom the idolators used to worship: (Was it you that they used to worship). Ibn Kathir: 3/520.\nWhat is the wisdom behind asking the angels about the worship of the idolators?\nوَيَوۡمَ يَحۡشُرُهُمۡ جَمِيعٗا ثُمَّ يَقُولُ لِلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ أَهَٰٓؤُلَآءِ إِيَّاكُمۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡبُدُونَ ٤٠\nThe testimony to nullify all deities besides Allah will be limited to the angels, since nullifying the deity of the angels will surely nullify that of everything else below them. This testimony will be the most important part of the Last Day's gathering. Ibn Ashur: 22/222.\nWhat is the benefit of limiting the testimony against the idolators to the angels on the Day of Resurrection?\nوَكَذَّبَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡ وَمَا بَلَغُواْ مِعۡشَارَ مَآ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُمۡ فَكَذَّبُواْ رُسُلِيۖ فَكَيۡفَ كَانَ نَكِيرِ ٤٥\nMeaning: We have given the past nations power, blessings, and longevity (yet they rejected My messengers; how severe was My response), My reproach and destruction, so let these idolators be warned of the fate of past nations. Al-Baghawi: 3/611.\nWhat is the point of mentioning the fate of nations before Muhammad's (ﷺ) Ummah?\nوَكَذَّبَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡ وَمَا بَلَغُواْ مِعۡشَارَ مَآ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُمۡ فَكَذَّبُواْ رُسُلِيۖ فَكَيۡفَ كَانَ نَكِيرِ ٤٥\nMeaning: That you should contemplate the matter of Muhammad (ﷺ) with sincerity to Allah, without leaning to desires or whims. (Stand up), not on your feet, rather, take the matter seriously. Ibn Juzay: 2/209.\nWhen is standing up in a matter for Allah considered sincere? When is it considered false?\n۞قُلۡ إِنَّمَآ أَعِظُكُم بِوَٰحِدَةٍۖ أَن تَقُومُواْ لِلَّهِ مَثۡنَىٰ وَفُرَٰدَىٰ ثُمَّ تَتَفَكَّرُواْۚ مَا بِصَاحِبِكُم مِّن جِنَّةٍۚ إِنۡ هُوَ إِلَّا نَذِيرٞ لَّكُم بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡ عَذَابٖ شَدِيدٖ ٤٦\n(Then reflect): Have you known him to be a liar, insane, or corrupt; did he seek to learn magic from someone, did he learn tales and read the books, did he have a greed for your money, or can you produce one Surah the like of what he brought you? If you ascertain his truthfulness, after this reflection, then why are you stubborn!? (It is yours), you be my witness that this reward is yours. Al-Qurtubi: 17/330.\nWhat kind of reflection they are asked to do? Based on that, how can we know the Truth from falsehood?\nقُلۡ مَا سَأَلۡتُكُم مِّنۡ أَجۡرٖ فَهُوَ لَكُمۡۖ\nThere is also another matter that discourages people from following the one who calls them to the truth, which is the fear that he may take the wealth of those who respond to him and take it as payment for his call. Hence Allah explained that His Messenger (ﷺ) was far above doing such a thing, as He said: (Say, \"If I had ever asked you for a reward, it is yours\") for your following the truth. Al-Saadi: 683.\nIn this verse, Allah describes a sign of the truthfulness of preachers. What is it?\nقُلۡ إِنَّ رَبِّي يَقۡذِفُ بِٱلۡحَقِّ عَلَّٰمُ ٱلۡغُيُوبِ ٤٨\nAmong Allah's Attributes, (the All-Knower of the unseen) is singled out for mention to indicate that He is aware of the intentions, and the Prophet (ﷺ) knows that, and therefore, he would never dare to falsely claim that Allah had sent him to you. Ibn Ashur: 22/238.\nIn this verse, Allah's Attribute, (the All-Knower of the unseen) is singled out for mention. Why?\nwords\nيَدرُسُونَهَاThey study\nنَكِيرِMy reproach\nبِوَاحِدَةٍOne thing\nمَثنَىIn pairs\nجِنَّةٍMadness\nيَقذِفُ بِالحَقِّHe hurls the Truth against falsehood, and it destroys it"],[434,"§Saba, Fatir\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, make the Holy Quran the spring of my heart, and the light of my chest, the banisher of my sadness, and the reliever of my distress.\"\nRecall a forbidden word that you have said, then ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nList five attributes of the angels from the verses of the Holy Quran.\nguid\nKnowing that Allah is (All-Hearing) and (Ever Near) will give you the sense that Allah is Near and He answers your prayers.\nFrom now on, remain in obedience to Allah, and hold fast to worships before you will wish to do so, but you will be banished.\nReflect on the greatness of Allah's creation of the angels, yet they are submissive and humble to Him.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ تَرَىٰٓ إِذۡ فَزِعُواْ فَلَا فَوۡتَ وَأُخِذُواْ مِن مَّكَانٖ قَرِيبٖ ٥١\n(And if you could see when they are terrified) when they encounter death in this life or adversity sent upon them by Allah. It is said: The terror that they will face in their graves from the Blast. Al-Qurtubi: 17/333.\nWhen a disbeliever faces the terrifying truths, how will his state be?\nوَيَقۡذِفُونَ بِٱلۡغَيۡبِ مِن مَّكَانِۢ بَعِيدٖ ٥٣\nMaking conjecture so as to refute the truth, but there is no way they could achieve that, just as there is no way for one who throws something from a great distance to hit his target. Similarly, it is impossible for falsehood to overwhelm the truth or defeat it. Rather, falsehood may have the upper hand for a short while, when the followers of the truth are in a state of negligence, but when the people of truth pay attention and resist falsehood, it will be suppressed. Al-Saadi: 684.\nThe attempt to refute the truth by the people of falsehood is described as far-fetched. Why?\nوَحِيلَ بَيۡنَهُمۡ وَبَيۡنَ مَا يَشۡتَهُونَ كَمَا فُعِلَ بِأَشۡيَاعِهِم مِّن قَبۡلُۚ إِنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ فِي شَكّٖ مُّرِيبِۢ ٥٤\nMeaning: A barrier will be placed between them and entering Paradise. It is said that they will not be able to benefit from the faith then. Moreover, it is said that they will be prevented from going back to the life of this world and its enjoyment. Ibn Juzay: 2/210.\nWhat is the thing that the disbelievers desire but cannot reach?\nوَحِيلَ بَيۡنَهُمۡ وَبَيۡنَ مَا يَشۡتَهُونَ كَمَا فُعِلَ بِأَشۡيَاعِهِم مِّن قَبۡلُۚ إِنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ فِي شَكّٖ مُّرِيبِۢ ٥٤\nThis analogy serves as a reminder to the polytheists of Makkah of what befell those before them, in order for them to be certain that Allah's way of dealing with disbelievers is the same, and that their idols which they claimed as interceders with Allah would not avail them anything. Ibn Ashur: 22/245.\nWhat is the benefit of using analogy in this verse?\nٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ فَاطِرِ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ جَاعِلِ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ رُسُلًا أُوْلِيٓ أَجۡنِحَةٖ مَّثۡنَىٰ وَثُلَٰثَ وَرُبَٰعَۚ يَزِيدُ فِي ٱلۡخَلۡقِ مَا يَشَآءُۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٞ ١\nThis Surah begins with (All praise be to Allah), which indicates that attributes of Allah's greatness will be mentioned. Allah's actions are attributed to His Holy Name; His creation of the heavens and earth and the best therein of angels and messengers indicates that this Surah was revealed to affirm Allah's Oneness and truthfulness of the Messenger (ﷺ). Ibn Ashur: 22/248.\nThis Surah begins with (All praise be to Allah). Why?\nمَّا يَفۡتَحِ ٱللَّهُ لِلنَّاسِ مِن رَّحۡمَةٖ فَلَا مُمۡسِكَ لَهَاۖ وَمَا يُمۡسِكۡ فَلَا مُرۡسِلَ لَهُۥ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦۚ\n(Whatever mercy Allah opens up for people), it is said that Allah's mercy means rain and provision. (None can withhold it), no one is able to prevent it. (And whatever He withholds, none can release it thereafter): He is (the All-Mighty) in what He withholds, and (All-Wise) in what He sends. Al-Baghawi: 3/616.\nCan anyone withhold something decreed for you by Allah?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ ٱذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡۚ هَلۡ مِنۡ خَٰلِقٍ غَيۡرُ ٱللَّهِ يَرۡزُقُكُم مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَۖ فَأَنَّىٰ تُؤۡفَكُونَ ٣\nAllah alerts and guides His servants to His Oneness and that they should worship Him alone, for just as He is the sole Creator and provider of provision, so He should be worshiped alone with no partners or associates such as idols and false gods. Ibn Kathir: 3/525.\nWhat is the link between creation and providing of provision, and worshiping Allah alone?\nwords\nفَزِعُواThey are terrified\nفَلاَ فَوتَThere is no escape\nوَأَنَّى لَهُمُ التَّنَاوُشُHow could they attain faith in the Hereafter\nوَيَقذِفُونَ بِالغَيبِThey make far-fetched conjectures\nبِأَشيَاعِهِمThe likes of them\nفَأَنَّى تُؤفَكُونَHow can you be averted from His Oneness?"],[435,"§Fatir\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, let not worldly affairs be my main concern, or the ultimate limit of my knowledge, and let not Hellfire be my fate.\"\nRemember satan's enmity to you day and night, seek refuge with Allah from him, and be careful.\nRemove harmful objects off the road, or help a person in need with your effort or wealth for the sake of Allah.\nguid\nRejecting the Messengers is a consolation to the preachers faced with rejection.\nWhoever senses enmity, will maintain vigilance.\nAdhere to Sunnah and the right evidence, and beware of innovation and following whims and emotions, lest you be of those whose evil deeds are made appealing to them.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ إِنَّ وَعۡدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقّ\nAs His promise is true, you should prepare for it and hasten to fill your precious time with righteous deeds, and do not let anything prevent you from doing so. Al-Saadi: 685.\nWhat should you do when you know that Allah’s promise is true?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ إِنَّ وَعۡدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقّٞۖ فَلَا تَغُرَّنَّكُمُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَلَا يَغُرَّنَّكُم بِٱللَّهِ ٱلۡغَرُورُ ٥\nSaeed bin Jubair said: The delusion of the worldly life is when someone becomes distracted by its enjoyments and pleasures from working for the Hereafter until the time comes when he says, (Oh, I wish I had sent ahead [some good] for my life) [89:24]. Al-Qurtubi: 17/346.\nHow can someone become deluded by the worldly life?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ إِنَّ وَعۡدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقّٞۖ فَلَا تَغُرَّنَّكُمُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَلَا يَغُرَّنَّكُم بِٱللَّهِ ٱلۡغَرُورُ ٥\nThis verse mentions two delusions, first: A delusion from within one’s self, where he makes appealing the charming appearances in this worldly life, and assumes that they are good for him at first, without thinking about their harmful consequences, or that they are from satan. Second: A delusion that he receives from satan, and likewise, the delusion in this world is dictated by a person's own self or received from devils among mankind and jinn. Ibn Ashur: 22/259.\nThis verse warns against two delusions. What are they?\nإِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ لَكُمۡ عَدُوّٞ فَٱتَّخِذُوهُ عَدُوًّاۚ إِنَّمَا يَدۡعُواْ حِزۡبَهُۥ لِيَكُونُواْ مِنۡ أَصۡحَٰبِ ٱلسَّعِيرِ ٦\nSince the enmity of satan is inherent, therefore, it is an eternal one even if he were to be forgiven. Allah commanded that satan must be taken as an enemy, for if he is not, then the Muslim will be heedless of his schemes and deception. Take satan as an enemy necessitates disobeying him to avoid his schemes, and for his hatred of righteous deeds. Ibn Ashur: 22/261.\nAllah commands that satan must be taken as an enemy, and not to be forgiven. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ لَكُمۡ عَدُوّٞ فَٱتَّخِذُوهُ عَدُوًّاۚ إِنَّمَا يَدۡعُواْ حِزۡبَهُۥ لِيَكُونُواْ مِنۡ أَصۡحَٰبِ ٱلسَّعِيرِ ٦\nMeaning: Take him as an enemy by not following him, and by being obedient to Allah. Al-Fudhail bin Iyadh said: \"O liar, slanderer, fear Allah; do not revile satan publicly and befriend him privately.\" Ibn Al-Sammak said: How strange for one who disobeyed the benevolent [Allah] after receiving His benevolence, and obeyed the accursed after knowing his enmity. Al-Qurtubi: 17/347.\nHow do you take Iblees as your enemy, as you are commanded by Allah?\nمَن كَانَ يُرِيدُ ٱلۡعِزَّةَ فَلِلَّهِ ٱلۡعِزَّةُ جَمِيعًاۚ\nMeaning: O you who seek honor, seek it from the One in Whose Hand it is, for honor is in the Hand of Allah and can only be attained by obeying Him. Al-Saadi: 685.\nHow does the Muslim benefit by knowing that all honor belongs to Allah?\nمَن كَانَ يُرِيدُ ٱلۡعِزَّةَ فَلِلَّهِ ٱلۡعِزَّةُ جَمِيعًاۚ\nThis verse has three possible interpretations, first -which is the most probable-: Whoever wants honor, let him ask Allah for it, as all honor belongs to Allah. Second: Whoever wants honor by defeating Islam, all honor belongs to Allah, and therefore, he will be defeated. Third: Whoever wants to know to whom honor belongs, let him know that all honor belongs to Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/212.\nAllah explains the way for one who seeks honor. Explain.\nwords\nفَلاَ تَغُرَّنَّكُمُDo not let it delude you\nالغَرُورُThe devil\nفَلاَ تَذهَبDo not let yourself perish\nحَسَرَاتٍIn grief for them\nفَتُثِيرُStirs\nيَبُورُPerishes\nمُعَمَّرٍAn aged person"],[436,"§Fatir\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah! Grant me the sense of piety and purify my soul as You are the Best to purify it. You are its Guardian and its Protecting Friend.\"\nRead a book about the importance of the deeds of the heart.\nGive some of your money to charity, pray nighttime prayer tonight, or recite the Holy Quran.\nguid\nBeware of invoking other than Allah, the Almighty.\nAllah is closer to those with humble and submissive hearts.\nEnsure to learn and benefit from admonishment and reminding in order to be of those who fear Allah.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ تَدۡعُونَ مِن دُونِهِۦ مَا يَمۡلِكُونَ مِن قِطۡمِيرٍ ١٣\nMeaning: They do not own anything, small or great, not even the thin membrane of a date stone, which is the most insignificant of things. Describing specifically something that they do not own indicates a general meaning, which is that they do not own anything else either, so how can they be called upon when they do not own anything in heaven or on earth?! Al-Saadi: 686.\nWhat is the benefit for man to know that those of which invoked besides Allah do not own anything?\nإِن تَدۡعُوهُمۡ لَا يَسۡمَعُواْ دُعَآءَكُمۡ وَلَوۡ سَمِعُواْ مَا ٱسۡتَجَابُواْ لَكُمۡۖ وَيَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ يَكۡفُرُونَ بِشِرۡكِكُمۡۚ وَلَا يُنَبِّئُكَ مِثۡلُ خَبِيرٖ ١٤\nAllah reveals the reality of the idols in order to show their uselessness for the idolators in the worldly life, and that Allah will make the idols speak, in the Hereafter, to renounce their shirk, and deny calling them to do it or be content with it. Ibn Ashur: 22/283.\nAllah nullifies idols worshiping in worldly life and in the Hereafter. How?\n۞يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ أَنتُمُ ٱلۡفُقَرَآءُ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۖ وَٱللَّهُ هُوَ ٱلۡغَنِيُّ ٱلۡحَمِيدُ ١٥\nAfter much proof and admonishments were presented, it did not appear that the idolators would break with their misguidance, and the eminent among them may have felt self-importance and conceit that they were very much sought after to join the Muslim community, which would make them susceptible to the devil’s temptation of insisting on their shirk. Therefore, Allah informs them that He is the Self-Sufficient Who is Free of need for them, and that His religion will not be honored by the likes of them; they will perish, and Allah will bring forth [in place of them] a people who will defend Islam. Ibn Ashur: 22/285.\nWhat is the wisdom behind describing all mankind as in need of Allah?\n۞يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ أَنتُمُ ٱلۡفُقَرَآءُ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۖ\nAllah addresses all people and informs them about their real situation and that they are in need of Allah in all ways. They are in need of His bringing them into existence; if it was not for His bringing them into existence, they would not exist. They are in need of His giving them physical strength, faculties, and senses; if it was not for His giving them these things, they would not be able to do any deeds. They are in need of His providing them with nourishment, provision, and blessings, both visible and hidden; if it was not for His bestowing His bounty and kindness, and making things easy for them, they would not have attained any provisions or blessings. They are in need of His warding off harm from them, averting troubles, and relieving them of stress and hardship. Al-Saadi: 687.\nIs people's need of Allah limited to wealth only? List some aspects of their need of Allah.\n۞يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ أَنتُمُ ٱلۡفُقَرَآءُ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۖ وَٱللَّهُ هُوَ ٱلۡغَنِيُّ ٱلۡحَمِيدُ ١٥\nAllah affirms their need for Him, and that He is the Self-Sufficient, but not every wealthy is useful unless he is generous and giving. Allah mentions (Praiseworthy) to indicate that He is the Self-Sufficient whose wealth is beneficial to His creations, the Generous and Bestower upon them. Al-Qurtubi: 17/366.\nIn this verse, Allah’s Attributes, (the Self-Sufficient) and (Praiseworthy) are mentioned together. Why?\nوَإِن تَدۡعُ مُثۡقَلَةٌ إِلَىٰ حِمۡلِهَا لَا يُحۡمَلۡ مِنۡهُ شَيۡءٞ وَلَوۡ كَانَ ذَا قُرۡبَىٰٓۗ\nIbn Abbas (k) said: A father or a mother will meet their son, and say: \"O son, bear some of my sins for me,\" but he will reply: \"I cannot, for I have enough of my own sins.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/621.\nWho will bear your sins for you on the Day of Resurrection?\nإِنَّمَا تُنذِرُ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخۡشَوۡنَ رَبَّهُم بِٱلۡغَيۡبِ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَۚ وَمَن تَزَكَّىٰ فَإِنَّمَا يَتَزَكَّىٰ لِنَفۡسِهِۦۚ وَإِلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡمَصِيرُ ١٨\nMeaning: Warning will only benefit those who fear Allah, but warning should not be limited to them. Ibn Juzay: 2/215.\nDoes this verse imply that Messengers and preachers warn those who fear Allah only. Explain.\nwords\nفُرَاتٌFresh and sweet\nسَائِغٌPalatable\nأُجَاجٌSalty and bitter\nمَوَاخِرَTraverse their way through water\nقِطمِيرٍThe membrane of a date seed\nمُثقَلَةٌA soul burdened with sins\nحِملِهَاIts burden of sins"],[437,"§Fatir\ndeeds\nStarting today, make time -even if short- for reciting the Quran daily.\nPerform the five daily prayers in congregation from the opening Takbir.\nGive a charity out of your money secretly, and give another publicly, so others may follow your example.\nguid\nEffect the fear of Allah in your life to be truly among those of knowledge.\nRecite the Quran often with reflection.\nAlways remember that the deal which will suffer no loss is the one with Allah, the Almighty.\nrefl\nوَمَا يَسۡتَوِي ٱلۡأَحۡيَآءُ وَلَا ٱلۡأَمۡوَٰتُۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُسۡمِعُ مَن يَشَآءُۖ وَمَآ أَنتَ بِمُسۡمِعٖ مَّن فِي ٱلۡقُبُورِ ٢٢\nThe believer is like the living, while the disbeliever is like the dead. (Indeed, Allah causes to hear whom He wills), that is the guidance of Allah to whomever He wills. (But you cannot make to hear those in the graves), that is the disbelievers not listening to evidence and admonishments, hence, He likens them to the dead who lack feeling. Ibn Juzay: 2/215.\nThis verse presents an eloquent analogy between the disbelievers and the dead. Explain the similarities between them.\nوَمَا يَسۡتَوِي ٱلۡأَحۡيَآءُ وَلَا ٱلۡأَمۡوَٰتُۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُسۡمِعُ مَن يَشَآءُۖ وَمَآ أَنتَ بِمُسۡمِعٖ مَّن فِي ٱلۡقُبُورِ ٢٢\nThe biggest deprivation stemming from disbelief is being deprived of benefit from the most eloquent and truthful word, which is the Quran. Ibn Ashur: 22/295.\nWhat is the biggest deprivation for the disbeliever in this world?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ أَنزَلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءٗ فَأَخۡرَجۡنَا بِهِۦ ثَمَرَٰتٖ مُّخۡتَلِفًا أَلۡوَٰنُهَاۚ وَمِنَ ٱلۡجِبَالِ جُدَدُۢ بِيضٞ وَحُمۡرٞ مُّخۡتَلِفٌ أَلۡوَٰنُهَا وَغَرَابِيبُ سُودٞ ٢٧ وَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ وَٱلدَّوَآبِّ وَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ مُخۡتَلِفٌ أَلۡوَٰنُهُۥ كَذَٰلِكَۗ\nAllah mentions His creation of things and their opposites -from which the origin and substance are the same, yet there are variations and differences that are visible and well known- so as to demonstrate to people His perfect might and sublime wisdom. These variations offer rational evidence for the divine will, which singles out each one to have a particular color and description; for the might of Allah, as He has created them like that; and for the divine wisdom and mercy. Al-Saadi: 688.\nThe variation, forms, and colors of the creations reflect one of Allah's Attributes. What is it?\nإِنَّمَا يَخۡشَى ٱللَّهَ مِنۡ عِبَادِهِ ٱلۡعُلَمَٰٓؤُاْۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ غَفُورٌ ٢٨\nAr-Rabí bin Anas said: \"Whoever does not fear Allah, is not a person of knowledge.\" Ibn Masoud said: \"Fear of Allah, the Almighty, is sufficient as knowledge, and being deceived concerning Him is sufficient as ignorance.\" Mujahid said: \"The true Faqih is one who fears Allah.\" Al-Qurtubi: 17/375-376.\nWhat is the prominent trait that distinguishes the true student of knowledge?\nإِنَّمَا يَخۡشَى ٱللَّهَ مِنۡ عِبَادِهِ ٱلۡعُلَمَٰٓؤُاْۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ غَفُورٌ ٢٨\n(The people of knowledge): Those who are knowledgeable about Allah and His Sharia, where their fear of Allah is commensurate with the amount of their knowledge. As for other people of knowledge that is not related to knowing Allah, and His reward and punishment the way it should be, then their knowledge will not bring them closer to Allah. Ibn Ashur: 22/304.\nWho is the true person of knowledge?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَتۡلُونَ كِتَٰبَ ٱللَّهِ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَأَنفَقُواْ مِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ سِرّٗا وَعَلَانِيَةٗ يَرۡجُونَ تِجَٰرَةٗ لَّن تَبُورَ ٢٩\nThis verse includes the Quran reciters, since they recite the Book of Allah and establish prayer, even if they do not reflect on the Quran, as the recital itself has a share of the light of Allah’s Words. Ibn Ashur: 22/297.\nIs the reciter of the Quran rewarded even if he does not reflect on it?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَتۡلُونَ كِتَٰبَ ٱللَّهِ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَأَنفَقُواْ مِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ سِرّٗا وَعَلَانِيَةٗ يَرۡجُونَ تِجَٰرَةٗ لَّن تَبُورَ ٢٩\nThis proves that they are sincere in their deeds and that there are no bad intentions or evil aims behind it. Al-Saadi: 689.\nWhat is meant by: (hoping for a deal that will suffer no loss)?\nwords\nالحَرُورُScorching wind\nوَبِالزُّبُرِBooks with written ordinances\nنَكِيرِMy reproach and punishment of them\nجُدَدٌTracts with various colors\nوَغَرَابِيبُ سُودٌExtremely black color, like raven\nلَن تَبُورَIt will not perish or suffer any loss"]])